(window.TZ_CONTENT=window.TZ_CONTENT||{})["en"]={"taaruf.001": "About the Tehreek", "taaruf.002": "This is a non-political reform movement, free of sectarianism, which calls people towards the Shariah and the Sunnah in the way of Imam-e-Rabbani Mujaddid Alf-e-Sani (RA) and of its perfect spiritual guides (Murshideen-e-Kamileen): Shams-ul-Kaunain Khwaja Muhammad Abdul Khaliq Naqshbandi, Qadri, Suhrawardi (RA), Shams-ul-Arifeen Hazrat Sain Abdul Razzaq Khaliqi Naqshbandi (RA), and Imam-uz-Zakireen Sain Muhammad Azeemullah Razzaqi Naqshbandi (RA).", "taaruf.003": "Here there is no greed, no desire for fame or large numbers — only the pleasure of Allah and the reform of the heart and the self.", "taaruf.004": "Aims of the Tehreek", "taaruf.005": "Tehreek Ittiba-e-Sunnat Pakistan is a non-political Islamic movement, free of sectarianism, which every member of the Muslim Ummah can join. The basic aims of this movement are as follows:", "taaruf.006": "In this age of trials, when innovations (bid'ah) and superstitions are at their peak, to create in the Muslim Ummah a longing to avoid innovations and superstitions, and to learn, teach and act upon the pure Shariah and the Sunnah of Mustafa ﷺ, so as to attain the fear of God and the love of Mustafa ﷺ. In this regard, to arrange as much teaching and instruction as possible, and also to spread the message of the Shariah and Sunnah wherever one goes.", "taaruf.007": "To establish as many religious madrasas as possible to promote the teaching of the Shariah, the Sunnah and the Quran.", "taaruf.008": "To establish orphanages in order to create a spirit of serving humanity and to promote the care of orphans.", "taaruf.009": "Especially, to save the young generation from indecency and evil and bring them to the mosque for the five daily prayers in congregation.", "taaruf.010": "To hold as many gatherings of the remembrance of God and the remembrance of Mustafa ﷺ as possible, in order to end the innovations practised in daily life as well as at weddings and other occasions of joy and grief, and to promote the Shariah and Sunnah.", "taaruf.011": "To promote the true teachings of the perfect saints (Awliya-e-Kamileen) in the light of the Quran and Sunnah, and, by uprooting the fabricated teachings of fake, conjuring and hereditary peers, to restore freshness to the distorted face of Tasawwuf in the present age.", "taaruf.012": "To promote Durood and Salam and gatherings of dhikr and Naat in order to attain perfect love for the Noble Master ﷺ.", "taaruf.013": "To eliminate social and moral evils and to spread good conduct and moral teachings.", "taaruf.014": "To create among women an inclination towards Shar'i purdah and obedience to their husbands, instead of fashion-worship.", "taaruf.015": "To create a spirit of love and loyalty for the whole Muslim world, and especially for our beloved homeland Pakistan.", "taaruf.016": "To promote offering prayer at its earliest time. Nowadays the Fajr and Zuhr prayers are offered very late in the mosques, which is negligence of prayer, whereas according to the Hanafi timings the time begins much earlier.", "taaruf.017": "To protect the honour of the Prophethood (Namoos-e-Risalat) and the Finality of Prophethood (Khatm-e-Nabuwat), and to expose the conspiracies of the Jews, the Hindus and the Qadianis.", "taaruf.018": "Following the Messenger ﷺ (Ittiba-e-Rasool)", "taaruf.019": "In the light of the Holy Quran", "taaruf.020": "In Surah Aal-e-Imran, Allah Almighty says: <span class=\"kk-ar\" style=\"display:block\">قُلْ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ تُحِبُّوْنَ اللّٰهَ فَاتَّبِعُوْنِيْ يُحْبِبْكُمُ اللّٰهُ وَيَغْفِرْ لَكُمْ ذُنُوْبَكُمْ</span>(Say: If you love Allah, then follow me; Allah will love you and forgive you all your sins.) The Prophet ﷺ is the Beloved of Allah Almighty, and a lover also makes his beloved that person in whom he sees the habits and traits of his own beloved. Therefore, striving to follow the Prophet ﷺ leads to the station of being beloved and wipes away sins. It is obligatory on every wise and sensible person to strive for perfect obedience to the Prophet ﷺ, outwardly and inwardly.", "taaruf.021": "In Surah Al-Ahzab He said: <span class=\"kk-ar\" style=\"display:block\">لَقَدْ كَانَ لَكُمْ فِيْ رَسُوْلِ اللّٰهِ اُسْوَةٌ حَسَنَةٌ لِّمَنْ كَانَ يَرْجُوا اللّٰهَ وَالْيَوْمَ الْاٰخِرَ وَذَكَرَ اللّٰهَ كَثِيْرًا</span>(Indeed, in the Messenger of Allah ﷺ you have the best example, for whoever hopes in Allah and the Last Day and remembers Allah abundantly.) So whoever turns to Allah, wishes to prepare for the Hereafter and also remembers Allah abundantly should follow the radiant way of the Holy Prophet ﷺ in every single aspect of life.", "taaruf.022": "In Surah An-Nisa He said: <span class=\"kk-ar\" style=\"display:block\">مَنْ يُّطِعِ الرَّسُوْلَ فَقَدْ اَطَاعَ اللّٰهَ</span>(Whoever obeys the Messenger ﷺ has indeed obeyed Allah, the Truth.) We learn that Allah Almighty has kept obedience to Himself hidden within obedience to His Beloved ﷺ. Obedience to the Messenger is itself obedience to Allah, and the remembrance of the Messenger ﷺ is the very remembrance of God. Now whoever regards obedience to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ as separate from obedience to Allah Almighty is a denier of the Quran.", "taaruf.023": "<b>Obedience to the Messenger ﷺ is the means of companionship with Allah's close servants:</b> In Surah An-Nisa, the Divine command is: <span class=\"kk-ar\" style=\"display:block\">وَمَنْ يُّطِعِ اللّٰهَ وَالرَّسُوْلَ فَاُولٰٓئِكَ مَعَ الَّذِيْنَ اَنْعَمَ اللّٰهُ عَلَيْهِمْ مِّنَ النَّبِيّٖنَ وَالصِّدِّيْقِيْنَ وَالشُّهَدَآءِ وَالصّٰلِحِيْنَ ۚ وَحَسُنَ اُولٰٓئِكَ رَفِيْقًا</span>(Whoever obeys Allah and His Messenger ﷺ, they will be with those upon whom Allah Almighty has bestowed favour — the Prophets, the truthful (Siddiqin), the martyrs and the righteous — and how excellent these are as companions.)", "taaruf.024": "<b>Without obedience to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, deeds are wasted:</b> In Surah Muhammad, the Divine saying is: <span class=\"kk-ar\" style=\"display:block\">يٰٓاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْٓا اَطِيْعُوا اللّٰهَ وَاَطِيْعُوا الرَّسُوْلَ وَلَا تُبْطِلُوْٓا اَعْمَالَكُمْ</span>(O you who believe! Obey Allah and obey the Messenger ﷺ, and do not render your deeds vain.)", "taaruf.025": "<b>Obedience to the Messenger ﷺ is the means of Divine mercy:</b> In Surah Aal-e-Imran it is stated: <span class=\"kk-ar\" style=\"display:block\">وَاَطِيْعُوا اللّٰهَ وَالرَّسُوْلَ لَعَلَّكُمْ تُرْحَمُوْنَ</span>(Obey Allah and His Messenger ﷺ so that you may be shown mercy.)", "taaruf.026": "<b>Obedience to the Messenger ﷺ is the cause of success in both worlds:</b> <span class=\"kk-ar\" style=\"display:block\">وَمَنْ يُّطِعِ اللّٰهَ وَرَسُوْلَهٗ فَقَدْ فَازَ فَوْزًا عَظِيْمًا</span>And whoever obeys Allah and His Messenger ﷺ has certainly attained a great success. (Surah Al-Ahzab)", "taaruf.027": "In verse 51 of Surah An-Nur, the quality of the successful believers is described: (The response of the believers, when they are called to Allah and His Messenger ﷺ in a matter so that he may judge between them, is that they say: We hear and we obey; and it is they who are the successful.) In the next verse He said: <span class=\"kk-ar\" style=\"display:block\">وَمَنْ يُّطِعِ اللّٰهَ وَرَسُوْلَهٗ وَيَخْشَ اللّٰهَ وَيَتَّقْهِ فَاُولٰٓئِكَ هُمُ الْفَآئِزُوْنَ</span>(And whoever obeys Allah and His Messenger ﷺ, fears Allah and adopts taqwa — it is they who are the successful.) In explaining this verse, Hazrat Umar (RA) said: the person who obeys Allah Almighty in the obligatory duties and follows the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the Sunnahs, fears Allah Almighty because of past mistakes, and avoids disobedience to Allah in the life to come — such people are the successful; and the successful one is he who is saved from the fire of Hell and admitted into Paradise. (Zia-ul-Quran)", "taaruf.028": "In Surah Al-Anfal He said: O you who believe! Respond to Allah and the Messenger ﷺ when the Messenger calls you to that which will give you life. (24). The call of the Prophet ﷺ is itself the call of Allah Almighty.", "taaruf.029": "In Surah Al-Hashr, the Divine command is: And whatever the Messenger ﷺ gives you, take it, and whatever he forbids you, refrain from it, and fear Allah. (7). From this noble verse we learn that obedience to the Prophet ﷺ — that is, acting upon the commands of Allah and refraining from what is forbidden — is obligatory; Allah will severely punish whoever disobeys the Prophet ﷺ.", "taaruf.030": "In the light of the blessed Ahadith", "taaruf.031": "<span class=\"kk-ar\" style=\"display:block\">خَيْرُ الْهُدٰى هُدٰى مُحَمَّدٍ ﷺ</span>The best way is the way of Hazrat Muhammad ﷺ. (Bukhari)", "taaruf.032": "The Prophet Mustafa ﷺ said: Whoever turns away from my Sunnah or deliberately abandons it is not from us, nor will he be worthy of intercession on the Day of Judgement. And whoever loves my Sunnah loves me, and whoever loves me will be with me in Paradise. (Tirmidhi)", "taaruf.033": "Every person of my Ummah will enter Paradise except the one who refused me (he will not enter Paradise). When asked, he said: Whoever disobeyed me has refused me. The Quran bears witness to this: On that day the wrongdoer will bite his hands and say: Alas! Would that I had taken the path of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ; woe to me! Would that I had not taken so-and-so as a friend. (Surah Al-Furqan: 27)", "taaruf.034": "The Holy Prophet ﷺ prayed: May the mercy of Allah Almighty be upon my successors. Someone asked: Who are your successors? He said: Those who love my Sunnah and teach it to the servants of Allah Almighty. (Jami' Bayan al-'Ilm wa Fadlihi)", "taaruf.035": "Before his passing he said: I am leaving among you two things; as long as you hold firmly to these two you will not go astray — one is the Book of Allah and the other is the Sunnah of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. (Bukhari, Kitab al-Ahkam)", "taaruf.036": "In the light of the sayings of the great elders", "taaruf.037": "<b>Sani-Isnain, Sayyiduna Siddiq-e-Akbar (may Allah be pleased with him):</b> After becoming the first Caliph, he said in his historic sermon: As long as I obey Allah Almighty and His Messenger ﷺ, obey me; and if I go against them, leave me. He had a perfect longing to follow the Messenger ﷺ. This can be gauged from the conversation that took place a few hours before his blessed passing between him and his dear daughter, Umm-ul-Momineen Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (RA). He said: Aisha! In how many cloths did you shroud the Messenger of God ﷺ? She replied: In three white cloths, among which there was neither a shirt nor a turban. He said: On which day did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ pass away? She replied: On Monday. He said: What day is today? She replied: Monday. He said: I hope that my death will be between now and tonight. And by Divine grace it happened just so: Allah, the Lord of Honour, granted him the honour of following the Messenger ﷺ even at the time of his passing, and he passed away on a Monday at the blessed age of sixty-three. He used to say: Any act that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to do, I do not leave without doing it; if I abandon any act from the practice of the Prophet ﷺ, I fear that I will deviate from the Sunnah of the Messenger ﷺ.", "taaruf.038": "<b>Sultan-ul-Arifeen Hazrat Bayazid Bustami (RA):</b> He learned about a man who had always stood in prayer by night and fasted by day. He said: Through spiritual struggle he has created the qualities of angels within himself, but this is no station, nor is it sainthood (wilayat); rather, the perfection of sainthood is to create within oneself the qualities of Muhammad ﷺ, that is, to mould all the moments of one's life — one's standing in prayer and fasting, one's speech and food — according to the Sunnah of Mustafa ﷺ. The path of the Shariah is even finer and more dangerous than the Bridge of Sirat, so one should never step outside the limits of the Shariah in any condition.", "taaruf.039": "<b>Sayyid-ut-Taifa Shaikh Junaid Baghdadi (RA):</b> He says that only he can truly follow the Shariah who holds the Holy Quran in his right hand and the Sunnah of Mustafa ﷺ in his left, and travels the path in the light of these two lamps, so that he neither falls into the pits of doubt nor gets trapped in the darkness of innovation.", "taaruf.040": "<b>Ghaus-e-Zaman Shaikh Abul Qasim Gurgani (RA):</b> He says that walking on the surface of water, flying in the air, and knowing and telling things of the unseen — none of these can be called a karamat (miracle of a saint), because all of this can also be possible with the help of Satan; indeed, how many soothsayers there are who tell things of the unseen. Rather, the greatest karamat is that a person becomes the very embodiment of Allah's command and submits to the Shariah with body, mind and wealth, and not even a trace of violating the rules of the Shariah is seen in any of his acts or movements. If this is his condition, then he is trustworthy. In following the Shariah, if you cannot ride a lion, there is no harm, because overpowering that dog of anger and rage — that is, the nafs (self) present in your breast — is far superior to riding many lions. Gaining awareness of the deceptions and tricks of the nafs is the greatest knowledge of the unseen. Going beyond the circle of the senses and imagination is no less than walking on water and flying in the air. Moving on, free of the greed of the world and worldly pursuits, and rejecting a single doubtful dirham is no less than leaping across vast plains and forests and crossing a difficult mountain pass — for Allah, the Truth, has named these obstacles ‘passes’ in His Holy Word.", "taaruf.041": "<b>Hazrat Data Ganj Bakhsh Hujwiri (RA):</b> Declaring adherence to the Shariah essential for spiritual progress, he says that the first pillar of the Shariah is the Book, as God Almighty says: In the Holy Quran there are clear (muhkam) verses; they are the foundation of the Book. (Surah Aal-e-Imran: 7). The second pillar is the Sunnah of the Messenger ﷺ, whose source is the Ahadith, as it is in the Holy Quran: And act upon what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ has said, and refrain from what he has forbidden. (Surah Al-Hashr). The third pillar is the consensus (ijma) of the Ummah, for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: My Ummah does not unite upon misguidance; always hold to the great majority (Sawad-e-Azam). From this the permissibility of taqlid also becomes clear. No Sufi can separate the Shariah from the Haqiqah (Reality). Sufi teachings are entirely subordinate to the commands of the Shariah. Therefore Tariqah is in fact the name of finding the Shariah itself in the depths of one's life.", "taaruf.042": "<b>Ghaus-ul-Azam Muhyiddin Shaikh Abdul Qadir Jilani (RA):</b> He said: Enter the darkness carrying a lamp, and that lamp is the Book of Allah and the blessed Sunnah of the Holy Prophet ﷺ. Never step outside the commands of the Book and the Sunnah. If any passing thought arises in your heart — such as fornication, usury, or mixing with the sinful and wicked — or an inspiration (ilham) occurs, then examine it in the light of the Book and the Sunnah; if you find it forbidden in the Book and the Sunnah, do not accept it, keep away from it, and be certain that it is from the accursed Satan. Because of guarding the limits of the Shariah, the servant becomes like that slave to whom the master entrusts all affairs. (Futuh al-Ghaib)", "taaruf.043": "<b>Shaikh-ush-Shuyukh Shaikh Shahabuddin Umar Suhrawardi (RA):</b> The founder of the Suhrawardi order and the spiritual guide of Hazrat Bahauddin Zakariya (RA), he says in his book Awarif al-Ma'arif that the Noble Messenger ﷺ said: By the One in whose hand is my soul! The people beloved to Allah Almighty are those who awaken the feeling of Divine love among His servants and strive to make them beloved to Allah; indeed, they are actively engaged in seeking the good of every person on the face of the earth. In this hadith the qualities of the noble Mashaikh are described. The Shaikh, acting as the deputy of the Prophets in calling to Allah, creates the love of Allah in his disciple in such a way that he sets him on the path of following and obeying the Noble Messenger ﷺ and leads him on the path of purifying the self (tazkiya-e-nafs). Thus whoever follows the Noble Messenger ﷺ in the correct way, Allah too begins to love him.", "taaruf.044": "<b>Imam-ut-Tariqat Khwaja-e-Khwajgan Sayyid Muhammad Bahauddin Naqshband (RA):</b> The foundation of our way is following the Ahadith and the traditions (athar) of the predecessors, and our aim is that our spiritual journey (suluk) be based on following the Sunnah of the Messenger ﷺ and that truth be distinguished from falsehood. The elect of God are those who follow the pure Shariah and complete their lives upon the creed of the Ahl-e-Sunnat wal-Jama'at. Even if, in spiritual exercise, your back bends and your body becomes like a bow, and you succeed in the exercise, yet as long as you do not purify your morsel and your clothing and do not follow the Shariah of the Messenger ﷺ, you will not reach the destination. Therefore all matters depend upon this. (Anis-ut-Talibin)", "taaruf.045": "<b>Imam-e-Rabbani Mahboob-e-Subhani Hazrat Mujaddid Alf-e-Sani (RA):</b> He says that the Shariah has three parts: knowledge, action and sincerity (ikhlas). As long as all three parts are not established, the Shariah is not attained. And when the Shariah is attained, it is as though the pleasure of Allah, the Truth, has been attained, as the Divine saying is: (And the pleasure of Allah Almighty is greatest of all.) So there remains no objective for whose attainment anything other than the Shariah is needed. Tariqah and Haqiqah, by which the Sufis are distinguished, are servants of the Shariah in perfecting its third part, sincerity. So the purpose of perfecting these two is the perfection of the Shariah, not some work other than the Shariah. Not telling lies with the tongue is Shariah, and removing even the thought of lying from the heart — that is, acquiring the habit of truthfulness without effort or artifice — is Haqiqah, that is, Tasawwuf. So Tasawwuf perfects the Shariah and does not oppose it. The sciences and gnosis that the Sufis attain on this path are not the real objective; rather, they are imaginings and fancies through which the children of the Tariqah are nurtured. One must pass beyond all of these and reach the station of Rida (contentment), because this is the highest station of jazba and suluk. Ignorant people, taking these manifestations (tajalliyat) and visions (mushahadat) to be the real objective, remain deprived of the perfections of the Shariah. Yes, reaching the station of sincerity and the rank of Rida depends on passing through these states and acquiring these sciences and gnosis. So these states and gnosis are causes and means for attaining the real objective. The Shariah is not subordinate to the states; rather, the inner states are subordinate to the Shariah, because the Shariah is definitive and established by revelation, whereas the states are conjectural and established by unveiling (kashf) and inspiration (ilham). So the group whom Allah, the Truth, has brought to the ultimate end (nihayat-un-nihaya) because of following the Prophet ﷺ never opposes the Shariah even by a hair's breadth in knowledge or action. And the divinely-given knowledge (ulum-e-ladunni) that descends upon them agrees with the Shariah; indeed, it is an elaboration of the sciences of the Shariah. Every kashf that goes against the outward Shariah is unacceptable, because it deviates from the path of the Prophet ﷺ. In Surah Ya-Sin the Divine saying is: (Indeed, you ﷺ are among the Messengers, upon a straight path.) It is astonishing that some deficient people regard their imaginary kashf as reliable and strive to oppose and deny the radiant Shariah, whereas even Hazrat Musa (peace be upon him), despite being the one who spoke with God and his special nearness, would have followed this same pure Shariah had he been in the world.", "taaruf.046": "In Surah Al-Baqarah it is stated: Those who believe are most intense in their love for Allah. (165). So the ability (tawfiq) to carry out the commands of the Shariah is the result of Divine love, and attaining inner composure is the fruit of this same love. If darknesses and impurities as vast as the whole world were cast into one's inner self but this love remained established, one should not grieve at all; and if lights and spiritual states equal to all the mountains were increased within but this love were reduced by a hair's breadth, one should regard it as nothing but ruin. The difference between the truthful and the false is known by steadfastness or lack of steadfastness upon the Shariah. The one who is truthful does not go against the Shariah even by a hair's breadth, despite intoxication, ecstasy and self-effacement. Maulana Rumi (RA) remained absorbed (in istighraq), yet at the time of prayer he would come back to his senses.", "taaruf.047": "The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: None of you will be a believer until his desire becomes subordinate to that which I have brought. So the wisdom in the obligations of the Shariah is that the commanding self (nafs-e-ammara) be ruined and humbled. The more one acts in accordance with the Shariah, the more the desires of the self decrease. That is why carrying out one of the commands of the Shariah is many degrees better, in removing the desires of the self, than thousand-year spiritual exercises and struggles devised by oneself; indeed, such exercises and struggles that are not in accordance with the Shariah give help and strength to the desires of the self. The Brahmins and yogis gained nothing from their toil and struggles except the strengthening and nurturing of the self. For example, offering the two rak'ahs of the Fajr prayer in congregation, which is one of the Sunnahs, is many degrees better than standing in prayer all night and then offering the Fajr prayer without congregation; eating food on the day of Eid-ul-Fitr by the command of the Shariah is better than fasting for many years by one's own choice; and spending one rupee as Zakat to humble the self is better than spending a thousand rupees by one's own will. In short, as long as the self is not cleansed and purified of the filth of seeking leadership, salvation is difficult and there is the danger of reaching everlasting death.", "taaruf.048": "A single particle of the approved following (of the Sunnah) is many degrees better than all worldly pleasures and the blessings of the Hereafter. Greatness depends on following the Sunnah, and excellence depends on carrying out the Shariah. Whatever is against the Shariah is rejected. Any ‘reality’ that the Shariah has rejected is heresy (zandaqa). Seeking the Haqiqah while keeping the Shariah firmly in its place is the work of the brave. After affirming the truth of the religion of the Prophet ﷺ, carrying out even a little action equals abundant action. The People of the Cave (Ashab-e-Kahf) attained such a great rank because of just one good deed, and that was migrating, with the light of faith, at a time when the enemies of God Almighty had prevailed; for at a time when enemies prevail, even a little effort is so prominent and worthy of regard that many times more action in days of peace cannot reach that regard. If outward migration is not possible, then, keeping inner migration in view, one should remain apart from people while living among them. On the Day of Gathering, they will ask about the Shariah, not about Tasawwuf. Entering Paradise and being saved from Hell depend on carrying out the commands of the Shariah. The very purpose of the creation of the noble Prophets is to convey the commands of the Shariah to people. So the greatest and weightiest good deed is to strive to spread the Shariah and to revive any one of its commands, especially in a time when the signs of Islam have been completely erased. And the person on whom the salvation of many people depends is better than the one who thinks only of his own salvation.", "taaruf.049": "The Divine saying is: (Indeed, this is My straight path, so follow it, and do not follow other paths.) The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: My Lord taught me manners and educated and disciplined me excellently. So if, during the journey, those travelling the path of Tariqah and Haqiqah commit acts that outwardly appear contrary to the Shariah, these are based on the overpowering of a spiritual state, that is, intoxication; and on passing beyond this station and returning to sobriety, that contradiction ends. The elders of the Muhammadan disposition (Muhammadi-ul-Mashrab) are honoured with the wealth of the Shariah and Sunnah, and the special Muhammadan sainthood ﷺ is their share. The most complete annihilation (fana-e-atamm) and the most perfect subsistence (baqa-e-akmal) are their distinction. And one who opposes this, even if he is among the Awliya and experiences kashf, has no share in this sainthood; he is on the footsteps of one of the earlier Prophets, and his knowledge accords with the Shariah of that Prophet. The Shariah of Muhammad ﷺ is the essence of all other Shariahs. Reaching this destination without following the Shariah and Sunnah is impossible. So congratulations to the person who has been honoured with this weighty blessing, and pity on the person who has remained deprived of this supreme blessing.", "taaruf.050": "Gratitude for the outward inheritance of the Prophet ﷺ is to be adorned with his inward inheritance, and being adorned with the inward inheritance is impossible without perfect following of the Prophet ﷺ. And the sign of perfect love for him ﷺ is to bear hatred towards the enemies of the Prophet ﷺ and to show enmity towards the opponents of the Shariah. Flattery is not permissible in love, because the lover is devoted to his beloved, and two opposing loves cannot come together. So it is necessary to spend all one's resolve in carrying out the commands of the Shariah, in honouring the scholars and Awliya who are people of the Shariah, and in keeping the innovators (bid'atis) humbled. Whoever honoured an innovator has, as it were, helped him in demolishing Islam. May Allah, the Truth, for the sake of His Prophet ﷺ, adorn and beautify our outward and inward selves with following the Sunnah of the Messenger ﷺ. (Maktubat of Imam-e-Rabbani Mujaddid Alf-e-Sani (RA))", "taaruf.051": "Our Requests", "taaruf.052": "The Spirit of Patriotism", "taaruf.053": "Love for one's homeland is a natural and good thing.", "taaruf.054": "So we should strive day and night for the exaltation of the religion of Islam and the stability of our beloved homeland Pakistan. Also, along with the fear of God and the love of Mustafa ﷺ, we should create the spirit of patriotism in the hearts of our children. The best way to do this is that, on the occasion of Independence Day too, the life stories of our forebears be narrated along with the remembrance of Allah Almighty and the Holy Prophet ﷺ. Furthermore, whoever performs his duties in any department should make truthfulness and honesty his hallmark; even the women and men who stay at home should fulfil their responsibilities in the best manner. To improve our society, we should take care of our neighbours and the poor and needy near us, and live our lives with love and affection, unity and harmony, and good conduct towards one another. Only a good Muslim can be a good human being and a good Pakistani.", "taaruf.055": "Lack of purdah and the negative use of mobile phones, and how to prevent them", "taaruf.056": "In Surah An-Nur the Divine command is: And (O Prophet ﷺ) tell the believing women to lower their gaze, guard their chastity and not display their adornment. (31). And He said: Stay with dignity in your homes and do not display yourselves as in the former days of ignorance. (Surah Al-Ahzab). And He said: Houris kept secluded in pavilions. (Surah Ar-Rahman: 72). In Paradise even the houris will observe purdah, where there will be no fear of any evil. In truth, purdah is the modesty and beauty of a woman.", "taaruf.057": "Today, in this age of trials, when lack of purdah and indecency are at their peak, we must together end this ugly custom of unveiling to protect the chastity of our pure daughters, and we must encourage our daughters and daughters-in-law to observe Shar'i purdah. The so-called enlightened women of today say that purdah is only of the gaze. When the female Companions observed purdah from the Noble Master ﷺ, and Allah Almighty commanded in His Holy Word to observe purdah from every non-mahram, what value remains in today's so-called enlightenment?", "taaruf.058": "Moreover! We must also protect our children, as far as possible, from the negative use of mobile phones. Today that very age has come about which the Prophet ﷺ said that trials will break through the doors of homes and enter inside. Mobile phones and television are that very trial through which indecency and evil have been able to reach children sitting at home. Today on WhatsApp statuses and social media nothing is seen except dancing, singing and idle amusement. For God's sake! Save yourselves and your families from that Fire whose fuel is people and stones.", "taaruf.059": "How you can become our helper in this good work", "taaruf.060": "If you agree with the aims and objectives of this movement of ours, you can contact our nominated workers, obtain the membership form and postal envelope completely free of charge, and become a member of this movement.", "taaruf.061": "If you do not wish to become a regular member, then support us by making whatever individual or collective effort you can on the requests set out in this booklet, for the spread of this movement.", "taaruf.062": "Source: booklet «Introduction to Tehreek Ittiba-e-Sunnat Pakistan and its Aims»", "baani.001": "Founder & Leader", "baani.002": "Founder of Tehreek Ittiba-e-Sunnat Pakistan", "baani.004": "Early Life and Education", "baani.005": "The founder and leader of Tehreek Ittiba-e-Sunnat Pakistan, Peer-e-Tariqat Karamat Ali bin Muhammad Ilyas Razzaqi, belongs to Goth Muhammad Abro, Sindh province. By lineage he belongs to the Rajput community. After his early education, he did a B.Com from New Aligarh College, Tando Adam, in 1983-84, and while in service he did an LLB after an MA in Economics.", "baani.006": "Employment", "baani.007": "In 1985 he joined Pakistan Post as a Senior Clerk. In 2013, as Assistant Superintendent Postal Services, by the order of his spiritual guide, he took retirement ten years before the fixed retirement age and became engaged day and night in spreading the exalted Silsila.", "baani.008": "Bait and Khilafat", "baani.009": "Coming from a religious family, he was inclined towards religion from the very beginning, and following his elders, in 1981 he took bait at the blessed hand of the great spiritual personality of the exalted Naqshbandi order, Qutb-e-Alam Hazrat Sain Abdul Razzaq (RA). At that time he was studying in college, yet he always kept a cap on his head and took special care to be regular in his prayers. Later he spent a considerable time, from time to time, in the service of his Peer-o-Murshid, Imam-uz-Zakireen Huzoor Muhammad Azeemullah Razzaqi Naqshbandi (RA), and benefited from his grace-filled company. In November 2006 his Peer-o-Murshid honoured him with his khilafat and deputyship.", "baani.010": "Religious Services", "baani.011": "Every year he arranges the blessed Urs on a large scale. Maintaining as much contact as possible with his fellow disciples (peer bhai), preaching the religion through sermons, and holding gatherings of the remembrance of the Beloved ﷺ are his way. He also makes positive use of social media to convey the message of the religion and the Silsila, and especially arranges online transmissions on the death anniversaries of the Rightly Guided Caliphs, the Ahl-e-Bait-e-Athar and the saints of the religion. Under this same mission he also keeps travelling to various regions of Pakistan.", "baani.012": "The management of Madrasa Arabia Khaliqia Razzaqia, established in his village in 1972, is also in his hands. In addition, he has built in his village Danish Kada-e-Azeem Markaz-e-Ilm-o-Irfan, which comprises the central office of Tehreek Ittiba-e-Sunnat Pakistan, the Mujaddid Alf-e-Sani (RA) Library, the under-construction Masjid Sayyiduna Siddiq-e-Akbar (RA), and a madrasa and orphanage for the religious and modern education and care of orphaned and deserving children. A separate madrasa for women has also been arranged. He also encourages other fellow disciples to establish madrasas as well as to arrange gatherings of dhikr and Naat.", "baani.013": "Method of Training", "baani.014": "Departing from conventional peer-murid practice, and exactly in accordance with the way of his perfect spiritual guides, he always teaches his disciples and every visitor Tawheed, the fear of God, reliance upon Allah (tawakkul), and love for and following of the Holy Prophet ﷺ. Along with establishing madrasas and religious education, he also makes special arrangements for modern education. Instead of books based on the kashf and miracles of the great Mashaikh — which certainly contain a considerable degree of exaggeration — he instructs people to read the own writings of those highly ranked Mashaikh.", "baani.015": "Writings", "baani.016": "To create further scholarly taste in the exalted Silsila, he has written and compiled more than ten books on Shariah and Tariqah. He has published a collection of his own Naats and Manqabats under the title «Huroof-e-Sana». He strives day and night to further promote this work.", "baani.017": "Written by: Engineer Shoaib Alam Azeemi Mujaddidi", "baani.018": "Introduction of the Sahibzadas", "baani.019": "Sahibzada Awais-ul-Azeem Azeemi", "baani.020": "He graduated from the University of Sindh and is currently serving in the Sindh Police as a Wireless Operator. He attends the gatherings and performs naqabat (hosting the gathering) in a very enthusiastic manner.", "murshideen.001": "The Spiritual Guides", "murshideen.002": "Shams-ul-Kaunain Khwaja Muhammad Abdul Khaliq Naqshbandi (RA)<span class=\"mk-hint\">Read introduction ▾</span>", "murshideen.003": "Companion of widows, helper of orphans, conqueror of Qadianism<br>Shams-ul-Kaunain Khwaja Muhammad Abdul Khaliq Shams-ul-Irfani Naqshbandi (RA)", "murshideen.004": "Early Life", "murshideen.005": "He is the son of Shams-ul-Irfan Khwaja Qadir Bakhsh (RA) and the Peer-o-Murshid of Shams-ul-Arifeen Ghaus-e-Zaman Sain Abdul Razzaq (RA). His title is Abu Sa'd. He was born at Jahankhelan on Friday, 7 Shawwal 1270 AH / 1854 CE, at the time of true dawn. He himself said that at the age of three he was called Qutb-e-Zaman among the angels, and at the age of seven the Holy Prophet ﷺ and all the noble Prophets gave him their blessed tongues to suck and said: We have given you all knowledge. He was only about three years old when his honoured father, Shams-ul-Irfan Khwaja Qadir Bakhsh (RA), was martyred.", "murshideen.006": "Acquiring Religious Knowledge", "murshideen.007": "For the knowledge of Hadith he went to Saharanpur to the service of Maulana Ahmad Ali Muhaddith (RA). Maulana Husain Ahmad Kanpuri (RA) and Peer Mehr Ali Shah Golrawi (RA) were his classmates. Later, in Delhi, he gained complete mastery of the religious sciences from Maulvi Karimullah Sahib (RA) and Maulvi Saeed Ahmad (RA). By the grace and favour of Allah Almighty he was a treasure-house of knowledge and excellence. Whenever any kind of issue was put before him, he explained it clearly with references in such a way that great muftis were left astonished. His khalifa Maulvi Abdul Karim Jasri Sahib (RA) writes in his book «Khaliqia» that Khwaja Sahib (RA) is a complete and most perfect person of the present age and a great scholar among the community of religious scholars.", "murshideen.008": "As a Preacher of the Religion", "murshideen.009": "He (RA) often delivered his speeches standing. His early discourses and sayings were based on guidance and instruction, encouraging religion and spreading Islam. When Allah Almighty commanded him to serve humanity, he was entrusted with the office of service and girded himself to serve the people, and in particular he carried out two services: the marriage of widows, and the service of orphans and the needy.", "murshideen.010": "Travels in Search of a Murshid", "murshideen.011": "From the age of six to thirty-five, most of his time was spent travelling. In this search he travelled throughout India, Afghanistan, Iran, Arabia and elsewhere. (He himself says:) I also reached Peer Pathan Shah Sulaiman Taunsvi (RA), Haji Imdadullah Muhajir Makki (RA) at the Holy Kaaba, and at Madinah Shareef the sahibs Abdul Ghani and Maulana Muhammad Umar (RA), and other elders; but I would ask for bait on the condition that if you cause ‘Allah, Allah’ to flow from my whole body, I will take bait. When the Mashaikh heard this request, they would withdraw their hand.", "murshideen.012": "Bait and Khilafat in the Qadri Order", "murshideen.013": "He says: When I reached Shaikh Ahmad Bukhari Qadri (RA) in Allahabad, on seeing me he said at once: «برو برو دیگر را بگیر» — go, look for some other way. I ran restlessly and clung to his feet. With great affection he raised my head and embraced me, and when the Shaikh (RA) took my hand in his blessed hand to give me bait and bestowed his attention (tawajjuh), I fell unconscious. At that time ‘Allah’ was flowing from every hair of my body. This is what the Holy Quran calls abundant remembrance (dhikr-e-kathir), and it is called Sultan-ul-Azkar.", "murshideen.014": "After six months of service, one day in front of all the dervishes the Shaikh wished to tie the turban of khilafat on my head and said: Is he worthy of this or not? Before anyone could answer, I submitted: Carrying this heavy burden seems very difficult, but with folded hands I implore that my heart's wish be fulfilled. He said: What is it? I submitted: Grant me your spiritual ecstasy (wajd). Hearing this, he (RA) said to all the dervishes: You people always used to say that the Shaikh loves this boy very much; now tell me, did the request this boy has made ever even occur to your hearts? Hearing this, all the dervishes went into ecstasy. He said: This is what is called understanding the secrets. Then, tying the turban of khilafat with his own pure hand, he said: Go, take bait in the Naqshbandi order and bring glory to the name of your honoured father; wherever you are, I will be with you.", "murshideen.015": "Bait and Khilafat in the Naqshbandi Order", "murshideen.016": "The Shaikh took him to Jalandhar and had him take bait in the Naqshbandi order from Haji Hafiz Mahmood Jalandhari (RA), the spiritual guide of his honoured father Shams-ul-Irfan (RA). Since his honoured father had left him the instruction to first sit at his shrine for seven years and serve both his own mother and his (the father's) mother, he would therefore come daily to the blessed shrine of his honoured father to complete the Naqshbandi path (suluk), and kept receiving spiritual training from the blessed shrine. He (RA) completed the Mujaddidi suluk in a short time, and Haji Sahib (RA) bestowed upon him the turban of khilafat.", "murshideen.017": "Services of Shams-ul-Kaunain in Reviving the Sunnah", "murshideen.018": "1. Marriage of Widows", "murshideen.019": "Khwaja Sahib says in his book «Sarmaya-e-Suhagan» that after four years of tireless effort, from 21 to 23 March 1892, corresponding to 1309 AH, he held a Jalsa-e-Islamia in the town of Kalanaur, District Rohtak, in which thirteen thousand seven hundred and sixty-five chairs were set out and a very large stage was decorated, on which the Deputy Commissioner of Rohtak, senior officials, and scholars and Mashaikh were seated. In the great households of Kalanaur, widows began to be married one after another. After thirteen hundred years, by persuading the Rajput community to follow this Divine command «Marry off the widows among you» (Al-Quran), he gained the honour of reviving the dead Sunnah of the marriage of widows. Before this, the Rajput community considered it a shameful act. A great deal of money was distributed among the poor and needy, and a Walima feast was also given to all.", "murshideen.020": "The notables had water and salt put into lotas (water vessels) and took a pledge: From today, with happiness and consent, we have abandoned this Hindu and un-Islamic custom and have accepted with heart and soul the command of God and the Messenger ﷺ. From now on we will always continue to arrange the marriage of widows. If anyone does not act upon this, all people will stop meeting and socialising with him and will cut off marriage ties with him. Whoever arranges the marriage of a widow, we will gladly take part in it, just as we take part in the marriage of a maiden; and whoever does not take part, considering it a disgrace and a reproach, the community (biradari) shall expel him. Just as we have established the second marriage of widows, in the same way we will establish Shar'i purdah, that is, we will strive hard, as far as possible, to have our daughters and daughters-in-law observe purdah from those who are non-mahram.", "murshideen.021": "2. Care of Orphans", "murshideen.022": "Wherever he (RA) went, along with preaching the marriage of widows he also urged the care of orphans, because orphans are closely connected with widows. He would say: The glad tidings that the Holy Prophet ﷺ gave to the one who cares for orphans were not given for any worshipper, ascetic, martyr or even the greatest righteous person. The Prophet Mustafa ﷺ said: I and the one who brings up an orphan will be together in Paradise like these two fingers. The Prophet ﷺ indicated this by joining the index finger and the finger next to it. Accordingly, whatever remained with him (RA), he distributed all of it among orphans and widows.", "murshideen.023": "On 15 June 1905 the Yateem Khana Khaliqia (orphanage) and the Anjuman Khaliqia were established. Then arrangements were made for teaching the Holy Quran. Later, a primary school was sanctioned in 1906, a middle school in 1914, a high school in 1925, and then an intermediate college. Hindu and Sikh children also benefited from these institutions. Children of Muslims, Brahmins, Banias, Sikhs and Chamars all studied there, and three orphan children even came from Africa for education.", "murshideen.024": "Likewise, Syed Ameer Husain Shah Sahib, resident of Rahim Yar Khan, transferred nineteen squares (murabba) of land to his (RA) name so that he could build a permanent (brick) khanqah for himself. But he (RA) transferred all that land to the name of his orphanage and said: We have no need of lands. He (RA) always kept his own residence in a mud house with a thatched roof, but had brick houses built for the orphans, travellers and school employees. If he met any officer who came to his door, he would shake hands with one hand; the gifts (nazrana) that officers presented he would not keep himself but would have them deposited in the orphanage, and would tell the officer: I have deposited your gift in the orphanage so that in return the Generous Lord may grant you a thousandfold in this world and the Hereafter. When any guest brought sweets and the like, following the Sunnah, he would distribute them himself with his affectionate hand among the orphans and dervishes.", "murshideen.025": "3. Protection of the Finality of Prophethood (Khatm-e-Nabuwat)", "murshideen.026": "When Mirza Ghulam Ahmad Qadiani made a false claim of prophethood, in 1902 thousands of Muslims gathered in Lahore for a mubahala (mutual imprecation). On behalf of the Ahl-e-Sunnat wal-Jama'at three persons were chosen — Shams-ul-Kaunain Khwaja Muhammad Abdul Khaliq (RA), Peer Mehr Ali Shah Golrawi (RA) and Anwar Shah Kashmiri (RA). Mirza Qadiani set the condition for the mubahala that a blank pen and inkpot be placed in the field, and nature would confirm his prophethood. These gentlemen accepted it. The next day people began coming to the field of mubahala in throngs, and these three elders also arrived, but instead of coming to the field Mirza Qadiani fled to Qadian.", "murshideen.027": "In December 1924 he (RA) was staying at the blessed shrine of Mujaddid Alf-e-Sani (RA) at Sirhind Shareef. The Muslims of District Rangpur, Bengal, wrote a letter saying that Mirza Qadiani's son, Mirza Bashir-ud-Din Qadiani, was challenging the Muslims to a mubahala; was he (RA) ready for the mubahala? He replied that he was ready for the mubahala on these conditions: (1) He himself should announce the date of the mubahala. (2) The place of the mubahala should be some major city of India, such as Delhi, Lahore, Calcutta or Bombay. (3) The mubahala should be held in a public gathering. When Mirza heard these conditions, he fled to Punjab.", "murshideen.028": "4. Establishing Prayer at its Earliest Time", "murshideen.029": "In 1925 he (RA) saw in a dream that a famous elder of the age was undergoing severe punishment. It became known that this punishment was due to offering prayers late and abandoning the congregation. From then on he began to hasten greatly in offering all prayers, especially Fajr and Zuhr, and, according to the timings of the Hanafi school, would arrange the congregational prayer as soon as the prayer time began.", "murshideen.030": "In Surah Al-Ma'un, Allah the Exalted says: <span class=\"kk-ar\" style=\"display:block\">فَوَيْلٌ لِّلْمُصَلِّيْنَ ۝ الَّذِيْنَ هُمْ عَنْ صَلَاتِهِمْ سَاهُوْنَ</span> — For those worshippers there is Wail, that is, the punishment of a pit of Hell, who are neglectful of their prayers. The Holy Prophet ﷺ said: Offering prayer at its earliest time is a cause of the pleasure of Allah, the Truth.", "murshideen.031": "Highly ranked Mashaikh such as Imam Ghazali (RA), Sayyiduna Shaikh Abdul Qadir Jilani (RA), Imam-e-Rabbani Mujaddid Alf-e-Sani (RA) and Shah Ghulam Ali Dehlavi (RA) also used to offer prayer at its earliest time and urged their disciples to do so as well. Moreover, every sensible person can well understand that, once the Lord's command has come, delaying the prayer without a Shar'i excuse is far from the claim of love and close to disobedience, whereas the beloved servant is the one who falls in prostration before his Lord as soon as the time comes. So one should strive to offer prayer at its earliest time.", "murshideen.032": "Blessed Passing (Wisal)", "murshideen.033": "At about one o'clock at night he woke Sain Sahib (RA) and said: Help me perform wudu and lead me in the Tahajjud nafl prayers. After the nafl prayers he fell into prostration and prayed: O Allah! Do not give me the pain of the throes of death, and grant me the rank of martyrdom in the state of prostration. After the prayer he said: Abdul Razzaq! Now I am very restless; keep pressing (my body). In this way the time of Fajr came; he (RA) performed wudu and offered the Sunnahs of Fajr. The congregation stood up. With him as followers in prayer were Syed Deen Ali Shah (RA), Sain Abdul Razzaq (RA) and Maulvi Sirajuddin. In the last prostration of the second rak'ah the entire roof suddenly fell, and on 7 Muharram-ul-Haram 1350 AH, at the blessed age of 80, he (RA) went to meet his True Creator.", "murshideen.034": "Shams-ul-Arifeen Sain Abdul Razzaq Khaliqi Naqshbandi (RA)<span class=\"mk-hint\">Read introduction ▾</span>", "murshideen.035": "Shams-ul-Arifeen, Siraj-us-Salikeen<br>Qutb-e-Aalam Hazrat Sain Abdul Razzaq Khaliqi Naqshbandi (RA)", "murshideen.036": "Kashf (unveiling) and karamat (miracles) are a lower-level matter; the real thing is following the Sunnah and adhering to the pure Shariah, because disciples are to watch the conduct of their guide and follow it. (Shams-ul-Arifeen (RA))", "murshideen.037": "He often used to say: The Shariah is the seed; if the seed itself is bad, how can the tree be sound? The beginning is Shariah and the end is Shariah. Even if someone comes flying through the air, but abandons the Shariah by even a hair's breadth, he may be a sorcerer, but he cannot be a friend of Allah.", "murshideen.038": "Blessed Birth", "murshideen.039": "According to his own sayings, his blessed birth took place in 1890. After his birth, his grandmother sent him to the mosque for good fortune and long life. He used to say that it is the favour of Allah Almighty that his whole life was spent in mosques.", "murshideen.040": "Early Education", "murshideen.041": "When he was five or six years old, he began offering the five daily prayers regularly, and from the age of seven or eight the Tahajjud prayer, which, by the grace of Allah, was never missed until his last breath.", "murshideen.042": "When you began the Tahajjud prayer, you were only seven years old.", "murshideen.043": "Neither the opening takbeer (of congregational prayer) was ever missed nor any prayer left unoffered; my beloved Sain (RA), how great you are!", "murshideen.044": "He received his early education at the Madrasa of Kalanaur. After the second grade he left school due to a state of divine absorption (majzoobiyat). He learned the Holy Quran from the mosque's imam, Hafiz Abdul Rehman Sahib.", "murshideen.045": "Presence in the Service of Khwaja Sahib (RA)", "murshideen.046": "The saints of religion say that whoever wishes to become close to Allah should keep the company of the friends of Allah (Awliya Allah).", "murshideen.047": "Accordingly, when he was twelve years old, his father took him to the service of Khwaja Sahib (RA). Khwaja Sahib (RA) took him in his lap and showed him affection. His father submitted: 'He keeps weeping all the time and reciting the Holy Quran, and does not speak to anyone; if only he would gain the sense to eat, drink, dress and speak.' Khwaja Sahib (RA) said: 'He will marry, he will have children, he will take up employment and he will also be a leader; his name has already been entered in the list of the accepted servants of the Holy Prophet ﷺ.' He himself used to say that what passed over him through the blessed gaze of Khwaja Sahib (RA) is beyond description. During this very period he took bai'at (allegiance) at the hand of Khwaja Sahib (RA).", "murshideen.048": "Traversing the Stages of the Spiritual Path", "murshideen.049": "Huzoor Sain Ji (RA) said: I remained in the service of Khwaja Sahib (RA) for 40 years, but never spoke in front of him. One day Khwaja Sahib (RA) was riding on my back and Syed Deen Ali Shah Sahib (RA) was carrying his blessed sandals. Weeping, he prayed thus:", "murshideen.050": "O Allah! As pleased as I am with this Abdul Razzaq, may You be just as pleased with him; and as much as he has served me, may the creation serve him just as much.", "murshideen.051": "Once Syed Deen Ali Shah Sahib (RA) submitted to Khwaja Sahib (RA): 'Huzoor! Had Abdul Razzaq been in the army, today he too would have been an officer.' He sat up and said: 'Shah Ji! What do you think? Army officers will lie at his feet.' He himself used to say: 'I have neither knowledge, nor did I turn the rosary, nor perform wirds and wazaif; all this is the grace of Khwaja Sahib's (RA) company, gaze, prayers and blessings. I never even raised my eyes to look before Khwaja Sahib (RA), nor ever spoke in his presence.'", "murshideen.052": "For thirty-six years you stayed with your Shaikh; beholding the Shaikh alone was your daily devotion (wazifa).", "murshideen.053": "Until your last breath you were never separated from him; my beloved Sain, how great you are!", "murshideen.054": "Care of Orphans", "murshideen.055": "In caring for orphans he had no equal. He always appeared restless and anxious to help and support the afflicted orphan children rejected by society.", "murshideen.056": "In this regard, Hafiz Aleem-ud-Din Sahib related that in 1965, when Huzoor Sain Ji (RA) returned from Hajj, many of us came from Dipalpur Sharif to Okara Station to welcome him. Mauj Din Razzaqi brought a garland of roses. We helped Huzoor down from the train. Mauj Din wanted to put the garland around Huzoor's neck, but Huzoor put that garland around Mauj Din's own neck and said: 'This is extravagance, it is showing off. It would have been better to deposit this much money in the orphanage.'", "murshideen.057": "He used to say that an orphan should be treated in such a way that he never feels even slightly that he is an orphan. If you are going to raise them by making them beg, then they can feed themselves too; what favour are you doing? Rather, having orphans collect donations and then using it yourself are both forbidden (haram).", "murshideen.058": "For the permanent rehabilitation of orphan children, he had orphanages named Dar-ul-Shafqat built at various places in the country at a cost of hundreds of thousands of rupees, along with mosques and educational institutions. Hundreds of orphaned and destitute children living in these orphanages were given modern and vocational education alongside religious education, and thus, instead of becoming a burden on society, they were enabled to live honourable and dignified lives. These institutions were duly registered and approved by the government, and examinations were held in them under the supervision of the Board.", "murshideen.059": "He had divided his ancestral agricultural land among his children so that they could live respectably, and gifted all the remaining urban property to the orphanage. Even before his passing, he deposited one hundred and twenty-three thousand rupees of offerings (nazrana) into the orphanage fund and said: 'If the children are worthy, they will build for themselves; if unworthy, they will waste even what they have. One should spend in the way of Allah, which will be of use in the Hereafter.'", "murshideen.060": "The Title Siraj-us-Salikeen", "murshideen.061": "Risaldar Muhammad Luqman Razzaqi Sahib relates that a question often came to his mind: how do the special servants of Allah Almighty receive various titles? One day, shortly before the Fajr prayer, I was sitting in the mosque when drowsiness overcame me. I saw that Imam-e-Rabbani Mujaddid Alf-e-Sani (RA) and Qibla-e-Aalam Huzoor Sain Ji (RA) were standing in front of the mihrab of the mosque. Hazrat Mujaddid Sahib (RA) embraced Sain Sahib (RA) and then said: 'Come, let us put upon you the seal of Siraj-us-Salikeen.' Then my eyes opened, and thus the question was answered.", "murshideen.062": "The Title Shams-ul-Arifeen", "murshideen.063": "Once he visited Muraala Sharif, at the place of Chiragh Ali Shah (RA), the khalifa of Syed Jamaat Ali Shah (RA), whose blessed shrine is in Walton, Lahore. Shah Sahib (RA) took off his turban, put it around his neck, raised both arms and said: 'What shall I tell you of who has come to my house! The Shariah forbids it, but understand it as if Narayan has come to the house of an ant.' At this Huzoor Sain Ji (RA) said: 'Shah Ji is a very great dervish; he is the master of a quarter of the world.' Shah Ji said: 'Sir, you have disclosed my secret; I beg your pardon, now I too cannot hold back, I too am disclosing your secret: you are the master of the whole world, and at this time you are the one and only.' Once Shah Sahib (RA) said that the title of Huzoor Sain Ji (RA) is Shams-ul-Arifeen.", "murshideen.064": "The Sorrowful Passing (Wisal)", "murshideen.065": "He was admitted to Kanaan Trust Hospital, Lahore, for a haemorrhoids operation, where his bed would be placed in the first row (of the congregation), tayammum would be done for him with earth, and lying down he would offer the congregational prayer with gestures. On 24 March 1982 he was again admitted to Kanaan Trust Hospital, Lahore.", "murshideen.066": "Finally, on Tuesday night, he entered a state of istighraq (spiritual absorption), and after remaining in that state for about 20 hours, at 4 pm on Wednesday, 31 March 1982, corresponding to 4 Jumada al-Thani 1403 AH, at the blessed age of about 95 years, he returned to his True Creator. At the time of passing he raised the index fingers of both hands, and at the same time the Name of the Essence, 'Allah', came from his blessed tongue. After his passing everyone saw that his sound heart was moving in the remembrance of Allah. Immediately after his blessed passing, Radio Pakistan Lahore announced: 'The sun of Tareeqat, after shining for about a century, set today, Wednesday, 31 March 1982, corresponding to 4 Jumada al-Thani 1403 AH.'", "murshideen.067": "The blessed body was given the ritual bath and, according to his will, wrapped in the sheet that was on Khwaja Sahib's (RA) blessed body at the time of his martyrdom, and Khwaja Sahib's (RA) blessed hairs were also placed in his shroud. Because of the huge crowd, his funeral prayer was offered three times. On Friday, 2 April, according to his will, the blessed body was placed in a suspended position in a wooden box and laid to rest.", "murshideen.068": "The Honourable Khulafa and Sajjadgan", "murshideen.069": "His three well-known khulafa (successors) are as follows:", "murshideen.070": "1. Imam-uz-Zakireen Huzoor Sain Muhammad Azeemullah Razzaqi Naqshbandi (RA), Darbar-e-Aalia Azeem Nagar Sharif, District Bahawalnagar.<br>2. Be-Had Sohne Khwaja Noor Ahmad Khan Razzaqi Naqshbandi (RA), Darbar-e-Aalia Lala Musa Sharif, District Gujrat.<br>3. Advocate Huzoor Muhammad Sharif Razzaqi Naqshbandi (RA), Darbar-e-Aalia Seil Gaon, District Pakpattan Sharif.", "murshideen.071": "He had two sons, whose names are as follows:", "murshideen.072": "1. Sahibzada Faqeer Muhammad Razzaqi Naqshbandi — may Allah Almighty keep his shade over our heads for a long time.<br>2. Sahibzada Bilal Ahmad Razzaqi Naqshbandi (RA). He passed away in 2025. May Allah Almighty elevate his ranks.", "murshideen.073": "Imam-uz-Zakireen Sain Muhammad Azeemullah Razzaqi Naqshbandi (RA)<span class=\"mk-hint\">Read introduction ▾</span>", "murshideen.074": "Imam-uz-Zakireen, Siraj-us-Salikeen, Qutb-e-Dauran<br>Mazhar-e-Noor-e-Khuda Qibla-e-Aalam Sain Muhammad Azeemullah Razzaqi Naqshbandi (RA)", "murshideen.075": "Birth and Childhood", "murshideen.076": "According to his identity card, he was born on 1 January 1934 in the village of Sehwani, District Hisar, India, in the home of Haji Hussain Ali Sahib (RA), a pious member of a Rajput family. His respected mother belonged to Mohalla Mir Khan of Dhankot, whose family now resides in Goth Muhammad Abro. In childhood he was often ill, and would stay silent or keep weeping.", "murshideen.077": "Bai'at-e-Tareeqat (Spiritual Allegiance)", "murshideen.078": "In Surah Al-Ma'idah, Allah Almighty says: <span class=\"kk-ar\" style=\"display:block\">يٰٓاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوا اتَّقُوا اللّٰهَ وَابْتَغُوْٓا اِلَيْهِ الْوَسِيْلَةَ وَجَاهِدُوْا فِيْ سَبِيْلِهٖ لَعَلَّكُمْ تُفْلِحُوْنَ</span> O you who believe! Fear Allah, seek the means (waseelah) to Him, and strive in His way so that you may succeed. (35)", "murshideen.079": "Our guide himself used to narrate the event of his bai'at thus: When I was studying in the fifth grade, army recruiters came, and I too was recruited along with other boys. In those very days Huzoor Sain Ji (RA) was staying at the dera of Rao Maratib Ali in Donga Bonga. I presented myself for ziyarat and Sain Ji (RA) accepted my bai'at at that very moment.", "murshideen.080": "Later, when Huzoor Sain Ji (RA) came to Sondha Sharif, my mother, on seeing him, said: 'This is the very saint whom an aamil in India showed me in my fingernail.' My mother stood in the way and submitted to Sain Ji (RA): 'I gave Azeemullah to you long ago.' Sain Ji (RA) said: 'Yes, he is mine.' In 1955 Huzoor Sain Ji (RA) took me with him to Dipalpur Sharif, and one day, while washing clothes, he sent for a lump of ochre (geru) and, along with dyeing his own clothes, dyed my clothes too in ochre colour.", "murshideen.081": "The Office of Khilafat", "murshideen.082": "He used to narrate the event of being granted the office of khilafat by Huzoor Sain Ji (RA) thus: Huzoor Sain Ji (RA) was seated in the Dipalpur Sharif mosque. After the morning circle of zikr, I went to the mosque courtyard and began cleaning wheat. After muraqaba, Huzoor Sain Ji (RA) called for me, took me in the embrace of his right arm and said: 'Make people do Allah Allah (zikr).' I submitted: 'Huzoor, everyone does Allah Allah very well.' He said: 'First make all of them your mureeds, then teach them Allah Allah.' At that moment great awe came over me and my whole body broke into sweat. He said: 'Khwaja Sahib (RA) told me in the same way: give tawajjuh like this, and make people do Allah Allah like this.'", "murshideen.083": "The Title Imam-uz-Zakireen", "murshideen.084": "This humble author had to get posters printed in my village for the annual Urs of Huzoor Sain Ji (RA). I fell asleep in this dilemma about what title, worthy of his status, to have written with the blessed name of Huzoor Qibla-e-Aalam (RA). In a dream I saw that this humble one was standing near the radiant grave of Huzoor Sain Ji (RA), and around his shrine, as far as my sight reached, from the floor to the Throne there was nothing but light, and a voice came from his radiant grave: 'Azeemullah! He is Imam-uz-Zakireen.'", "murshideen.085": "Blessed Passing (Wisal)", "murshideen.086": "After a long illness, on 14 Jumada al-Awwal 1434 AH, corresponding to 27 March 2013, on Wednesday at eight in the morning, in Sondha Sharif, while doing the zikr of Allah, he returned to his True Creator at the age of about 83 years. According to his younger sister Hukumat Bibi, near his passing he said that Huzoor Sain Ji (RA) was sitting beside him.", "murshideen.087": "He was buried on Friday, 29 March, on Bahawalnagar Road, at Suraj Ganj Morr shortly before Donga Bonga, near the courtyard of his mosque, where his blessed mausoleum is now under construction on the design of the blessed shrine of Sain Huzoor (RA). The creation of God is receiving his blessings day and night.", "murshideen.088": "Photos and details of the shrines will be added soon, In sha Allah.", "mubalighin.001": "Our Preachers", "mubalighin.002": "Photos and videos will be added soon, In sha Allah.", "markaz.001": "Main Markaz", "marakiz.001": "Centres & Madaris", "marakiz.002": "Islampur", "marakiz.003": "Kotli Najabat", "marakiz.004": "Vehari", "marakiz.005": "Kot Misri Khan", "marakiz.006": "Muhajir Goth", "marakiz.007": "Goth Abro", "marakiz.008": "35 Chak", "marakiz.009": "Rao Garh", "marakiz.010": "Details of the other centres and madaris will be added soon, In sha Allah.", "bayanat.001": "Bayanat", "bayanat.002": "Tap any bayan — the video plays on YouTube.", "kutub.001": "Books", "kutub.002": "Harf Harf Taseer", "kutub.003": "<span>Author:</span> Founder and Leader of Tehreek Ittiba-e-Sunnat Pakistan, religious scholar Karamat Ali Razzaqi Azeemi Mujaddidi Naqshbandi <span class=\"lat\">(M.A, L.L.B)</span>", "kutub.004": "<span>Assisted by:</span> Engineer Shoaib Alam Azeemi Mujaddidi (M.A. Islamic Studies), <span class=\"lat\">HOD</span> Electrical Trade, Government Technical Training Institute Lodhran", "kutub.005": "Pages: <span class=\"lat\">136</span>  • Published: October <span class=\"lat\">2026</span>", "kutub.006": "Introduction and Aims of Tehreek Ittiba-e-Sunnat Pakistan", "kutub.007": "Our aim: promotion of the Shariah and Sunnah", "kutub.008": "<span>Author:</span> Founder and Leader of the Tehreek, Peer-e-Tareeqat Karamat Ali Razzaqi Azeemi Naqshbandi <span class=\"lat\">(M.A, L.L.B)</span>", "kutub.009": "Pages: <span class=\"lat\">19</span>", "kutub.010": "Sirat-ul-Falah fid-Dunya wal-Akhirah", "kutub.011": "The Path to Success in this World and the Hereafter", "kutub.012": "<span>Author:</span> Founder and Leader of Tehreek Ittiba-e-Sunnat Pakistan, Peer-e-Tareeqat Karamat Ali Razzaqi Azeemi Naqshbandi <span class=\"lat\">(M.A, L.L.B)</span>", "kutub.013": "<span>Assisted by:</span> Engineer Shoaib Alam Azeemi Mujaddidi (M.A. Islamic Studies), <span class=\"lat\">HOD</span> Electrical Trade, Government Technical Training Institute Lodhran", "kutub.014": "Pages: <span class=\"lat\">83</span>  • Published: March <span class=\"lat\">2019</span>", "kutub.015": "Dastoor-e-Tareeqat", "kutub.016": "Also known as Raah-e-Sulook", "kutub.017": "<span>Author:</span> Founder and Leader of Tehreek Ittiba-e-Sunnat Pakistan, Peer-e-Tareeqat, Sher-e-Mujaddid Badr-ul-Huda Karamat Ali Razzaqi Azeemi Naqshbandi <span class=\"lat\">(M.A, L.L.B)</span>", "kutub.018": "<span>Assisted by:</span> Engineer Shoaib Alam Azeemi Mujaddidi (M.A. Islamic Studies), <span class=\"lat\">HOD</span> Electrical Trade, Government Technical Training Institute Lodhran", "kutub.019": "Pages: <span class=\"lat\">129</span>  • Published: October <span class=\"lat\">2016</span>", "gallery.001": "Picture Gallery", "bait.001": "Bai\\'at & Tariqat", "bait.002": "Bai'at-e-Tareeqat (Spiritual Allegiance)", "bait.003": "In Surah Al-Ma'idah, Allah Almighty says: <span class=\"kk-ar\" lang=\"ar\" style=\"display:block\">يٰٓاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوا اتَّقُوا اللّٰهَ وَابْتَغُوْٓا اِلَيْهِ الْوَسِيْلَةَ وَجَاهِدُوْا فِيْ سَبِيْلِهٖ لَعَلَّكُمْ تُفْلِحُوْنَ</span> O you who believe! Fear Allah, seek the means (waseelah) to Him, and strive in His way so that you may succeed. (35)", "bait.004": "Shah Waliullah Muhaddith Dehlvi says that in this verse 'waseelah' means a perfect spiritual guide (Murshid-e-Kamil).", "bait.005": "In Surah Luqman, Allah Almighty says: <span class=\"kk-ar\" lang=\"ar\" style=\"display:block\">وَاتَّبِعْ سَبِيْلَ مَنْ اَنَابَ اِلَيَّ</span> And follow the way of the one who turns to Me. (15)", "bait.006": "Regarding bai'at of tareeqat and iradat, Sayyiduna Ubadah ibn as-Samit al-Ansari (RA) says: We pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to hear and obey his ﷺ command in ease and hardship, in what pleased us and what we disliked, and not to dispute any command of his ﷺ. (Bukhari, Book of Judgments)", "bait.007": "Hujjat-ul-Islam Imam Ghazali (RA) says that apart from the noble Prophets (peace be upon them), no one is free of outward and inward ailments. Therefore, to remove these ailments it is necessary to enter the tareeqat in the company of the Sufis. Just as it is settled in medicine that despite reading medical books no one can treat himself on his own, but needs a physician for it; in exactly the same way, the ailments of the heart and the self cannot be treated on one's own — for these too a perfect spiritual guide is needed.", "bait.008": "Sayyiduna Abdul Qadir Isa Shazli (RA) says that even the noble Companions (RA) of the Holy Prophet ﷺ could not treat their souls merely by reading the Quran; they too were attached to the healing house of the Expert Physician of both worlds ﷺ, and he ﷺ purified their selves and cleansed their hearts. (Haqaiq 'an at-Tasawwuf)", "bait.009": "Our grand-murshid, Shams-ul-Kaunain, Fateh-e-Qadianiyat Khwaja Muhammad Abdul Khaliq (RA) says: The word bai'at comes from the word bai', which means to be sold. When a mureed takes bai'at, he hands over all his intentions to the Peer. Something that has been sold cannot be taken back without mutual consent; so how can he sell it elsewhere? (Lam'at-e-Kamalat-e-Qadiriyya)", "bait.010": "The Purpose of Bai'at-e-Tareeqat", "bait.011": "Imam-e-Rabbani Mujaddid Alf-e-Sani (RA) says that the Shariah has three parts: knowledge, action and sincerity (ikhlas). And tareeqat is the means of attaining the third part of the Shariah, namely sincerity. Thus tareeqat is not something separate from the Shariah; rather, it is the servant of the Shariah in perfecting the Shariah.", "bait.012": "Thus the real purpose of bai'at is ikhlas, that is, attaining the pleasure of Allah. Its means are: following the commands of the Shariah and the Sunnah of the Prophet ﷺ completely, remaining content with the will of Allah Almighty, not being greedy, keeping the heart present in worship, doing the works of religion with sincerity, not regarding anyone as inferior, being free of self-conceit, restraining anger, and remaining occupied in zikr and reflection. Adopting such character is called sulook.", "bait.013": "It should be known that in this neither kashf and karamat are necessary, nor is there a promise of success in worldly affairs, nor a claim of curing illness by incantations, nor knowledge of future events, nor are spiritual powers (tasarrufat) required such that the mureed will be reformed automatically by the Peer's attention; nor is there any fixed period for such inner states to arise that one is always — or at least during worship — filled with delight and ecstasy and no stray thoughts come in worship; nor is it necessary to see lights and the like or hear any voice in zikr and spiritual practice; nor is it necessary to see good dreams or for inspirations to be correct and accurate.", "bait.014": "Conditions of a Perfect Shaikh", "bait.015": "In these times forgery and trickery are at their peak, and the true face of tasawwuf is being presented in a distorted form. Therefore, incidentally, the five conditions of a perfect Shaikh are stated, so that seekers of the path may themselves distinguish the genuine from the fake and save themselves from going astray.", "bait.016": "Ala Hazrat Imam Ahmad Raza Khan Barelvi (RA) says regarding the conditions of a perfect Peer:", "bait.017": "<b class=\"az-n\">1. Belief (Aqeedah):</b> The Peer must be of sound belief according to the creed of Ahl-e-Sunnat wal-Jama'at, because the chain of a misguided innovator will reach Satan, not the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. (In these times, if a Peer's belief is against the superiority of the Shaikhain, i.e. Hazrat Siddiq and Hazrat Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both), or he does not hold a good opinion about Sayyiduna Ameer Muawiya (RA), then a Sunni mureed should immediately break bai'at with such a Peer and take bai'at with a Shaikh of sound belief.)", "bait.018": "Regarding soundness of belief, Qayyum-e-Zaman Mirza Mazhar Jan-e-Janan Shaheed Dehlvi (RA) says: Expressing love for the pure Ahl-e-Bait and equal reverence for the noble Companions (RA) is necessary. This is the Straight Path which will appear on the Day of Judgement in the form of the Bridge of Sirat; whoever does not deviate from this path in the world will pass over it steadfastly on the Day of Judgement. (Maqamat-e-Mazhari)", "bait.019": "<b class=\"az-n\">2. Knowledge (Ilm):</b> It is a condition that he has enough knowledge to find the rulings he needs from books without anyone's help. One can become a scholar through study and by listening to people as well. A graduation certificate is neither a condition nor sufficient; rather, there must be knowledge. He should be aware of the rulings of the Shariah — commands and prohibitions, lawful and unlawful, obligatory (fard) and necessary (wajib), Sunnah and recommended (mustahab), and disbelief and Islam — that is, the science of fiqh. And he should be able to read Arabic text well.", "bait.020": "Our grand-murshid Shams-ul-Kaunain Khwaja Muhammad Abdul Khaliq Shams-ul-Irfani Naqshbandi (RA) says:", "bait.021": "<b class=\"az-n\">3. Practice (Amal):</b> He should act upon his knowledge. No fard, Sunnah or mustahab should be missed by him, to the extent that he uses the comb and the miswak, prays in congregation and does not miss the Friday prayer. He should firmly practise the Shariah and not fall short in following Mustafa ﷺ.", "bait.022": "<b class=\"az-n\">4. Sincerity (Ikhlas):</b> Shams-ul-Kaunain Khwaja Abdul Khaliq (RA) says that every action of the Peer should be for the pleasure of Allah.", "bait.023": "<b class=\"az-n\">5. Chain (Silsila) and Khilafat:</b> The Peer's spiritual chain must be sound, that is, he must be the mureed of some Peer and have received khilafat, so that his hand reaches, hand to hand, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Whoever gives bai'at without khilafat is regarded by the people of tareeqat as a zindeeq (heretic), and he is astray. And some people, without having become mureeds, merely presuming themselves to be Peerzadas, sit as sajjada nasheen at the shrines of their forefathers. Or the chain itself is one that was cut off and in which no spiritual grace was kept, yet people keep giving khilafat in it out of greed; or the chain was sound but in between came a person who was not fit to be a Peer, and the branch that proceeded from him is broken in between. In all these cases, such a bai'at will never reach the hand of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and no spiritual grace will be attained, because milk does not come from an ox nor a child from a barren woman.", "bait.024": "Basic Qualities of a Perfect Shaikh", "bait.025": "It should be known that a perfect Peer must have the following five qualities.", "bait.026": "Sultan-ul-Arifeen Shaikh Bayazid Bistami (RA) says:", "bait.027": "<b class=\"az-n\">1.</b> The Peer should be of good character.", "bait.028": "<b class=\"az-n\">2.</b> He should be generous.", "bait.029": "<b class=\"az-n\">3.</b> He should be humble.", "bait.030": "Our Shams-ul-Kaunain Khwaja Abdul Khaliq (RA) says:", "bait.031": "<b class=\"az-n\">4.</b> The Peer should possess great character, so that the mureed's difficulties are easily resolved.", "bait.032": "<b class=\"az-n\">5.</b> At the time of bai'at, the Peer should make the zikr of the Name of the Essence (Ism-e-Zaat) flow from every hair of the body.", "mamulat.001": "Khatm-e-Khwajgan Naqshbandiya", "mamulat.002": "Issued by Mazhar-e-Jamal-e-Mustafai, Khwaja-e-Khwajgan, Hami-e-Bewagan (supporter of widows), Dastgeer-e-Yatama (helper of orphans), Fateh-e-Qadianiyat, Qutb-ul-Aqtab, Shams-ul-Kaunain Abu Saad Muhammad Abdul Khaliq Naqshbandi (RA)", "mamulat.003": "Note: Before every wird, be sure to recite Bismillah Shareef once.", "mamulat.004": "(I seek forgiveness from Allah, besides whom there is no god, the Ever-Living, the Sustainer, and I turn to Him in repentance.)", "mamulat.005": "Surah Al-Fatihah <span class=\"kk-c\">7 times</span>", "mamulat.006": "Durood-e-Khaliqiya", "mamulat.007": "(O Allah! Send blessings, equal to the totality of Your knowledge, upon our master Hazrat Muhammad ﷺ and upon the family and companions of our master Hazrat Muhammad ﷺ.)", "mamulat.008": "Surah Alam Nashrah <span class=\"kk-c\">79 times</span>", "mamulat.009": "Surah Al-Ikhlas with Bismillah Shareef <span class=\"kk-c\">1000 times</span>", "mamulat.010": "Surah Al-Fatihah <span class=\"kk-c\">7 times</span>", "mamulat.011": "Recite each of the following phrases one hundred times:", "mamulat.012": "Durood-e-Khaliqiya", "mamulat.013": "(The power to avoid sins and the strength to do good come only from Allah.)", "mamulat.014": "(There is no god but You; You are pure (from doing injustice); indeed I am among the wrongdoers, that is, I end up wronging myself.)", "mamulat.015": "(O Ever-Living, O Sustainer, by Your mercy grant help, O Helper of those who seek help.)", "mamulat.016": "(O Possessor of Honour! Make me honourable in the sight of creation.)", "mamulat.017": "(O Fulfiller of needs)", "mamulat.018": "(O Raiser of ranks)", "mamulat.019": "(O Remover of calamities)", "mamulat.020": "(O Opener of difficulties)", "mamulat.021": "(O Healer of illnesses)", "mamulat.022": "(O Answerer of prayers)", "mamulat.023": "(O Solver of difficulties)", "mamulat.024": "(O Creator of means)", "mamulat.025": "(O Self-Sufficient One who makes others free of need and rich)", "mamulat.026": "(O One free of need of and independent from everything)", "mamulat.027": "(O Creator in abundance)", "mamulat.028": "(O Giver of sustenance who bestows abundantly)", "mamulat.029": "(O Bestower of rewards and blessings)", "mamulat.030": "(O Self-Sufficient One! Who makes one free of need of all besides You)", "mamulat.031": "(O Most Loving)", "mamulat.032": "(O Most Merciful to everyone)", "mamulat.033": "(O Most Kind to Your special ones and those who love You)", "mamulat.034": "(O Most Generous)", "mamulat.035": "(O Forgiver)", "mamulat.036": "(O Most Pardoning and Concealer of faults)", "mamulat.037": "(O Remover of difficulties and Opener of the door of ease)", "mamulat.038": "(O Giver of everything)", "mamulat.039": "(O Giver of honour)", "mamulat.040": "(O Giver of elevation)", "mamulat.041": "(O Expander of provision)", "mamulat.042": "(O Flawless Being! Giver of peace and safety)", "mamulat.043": "(O True Disposer of affairs)", "mamulat.044": "(O Guardian! Who watches over creation)", "mamulat.045": "(O Lord of all the worlds)", "mamulat.046": "(O True Nurturer of all the worlds)", "mamulat.047": "(O True Lord of all the worlds)", "mamulat.048": "(By Your mercy! O Most Merciful of all who show mercy)", "mamulat.049": "Now recite the short Khatm Shareef:", "mamulat.050": "(O Allah! I seek Your forgiveness.)", "mamulat.051": "(O Allah! O my Lord! I seek forgiveness for every sin and turn to You in repentance.)", "mamulat.052": "Surah Al-Fatihah <span class=\"kk-c\">7 times</span>", "mamulat.053": "Durood-e-Khaliqiya <span class=\"kk-c\">11 times</span>", "mamulat.054": "Through the blessing of the Holy Prophet ﷺ, send the reward (isal-e-sawab) to all the noble Prophets (peace be upon them), the Rightly Guided Caliphs, the pure Ahl-e-Bait, the noble Companions (may Allah be pleased with them) and the great saints (Peeran-e-Izam).", "shajra.001": "Shajra-e-Tariqat", "shajra.002": "Despite having khilafat in all four orders (silsilas), our Murshideen propagated the exalted Naqshbandi Mujaddidi order. Therefore, the names of the saints of this exalted order are presented, for blessing, for the awareness of the general public.", "shajra.003": "Rahmatul-lil-Aalameen, Khatam-un-Nabiyyeen, Sayyid-ul-Mursaleen, Hazrat Muhammad Mustafa ﷺ<small>Passed away 11 AH — Resting place: the Green Dome (Gumbad-e-Khazra)</small>", "shajra.004": "Companion of the Cave and of the Tomb, verily the best of humans after the Prophets, Sayyiduna Abu Bakr Siddiq (RA)<small>13 AH — Green Dome, Madinah Munawwarah</small>", "shajra.005": "The pure Companion, companion of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, Hazrat Sayyiduna Salman Farsi (RA)<small>33 AH — Mada'in, Iraq</small>", "shajra.006": "Hazrat Sayyiduna Imam Qasim (RA) son of Sayyiduna Muhammad (RA) son of Sayyiduna Abu Bakr Siddiq (RA)<small>106 AH — Madinah Munawwarah</small>", "shajra.007": "Imam-ush-Shariah, Hadi-e-Tareeqat Hazrat Sayyiduna Imam Jafar Sadiq (RA)<small>148 AH — Jannat-ul-Baqi, Dome of the Ahl-e-Bait</small>", "shajra.008": "Sultan-ul-Arifeen, Ghaus-e-Zamani, Hazrat Shaikh Bayazid Bistami (RA)<small>261 AH — Bistam, Iran</small>", "shajra.009": "Qutb-e-Rabbani, Ghaus-e-Zaman, Khwaja Abul Hasan Kharqani (RA)<small>425 AH — Kharqan near Bistam, Iran</small>", "shajra.010": "Arif-e-Rabbani, Qutb-e-Zamani, Hazrat Shaikh Abul Qasim Gurgani (RA)<small>450 AH — Gurgan, Iran</small>", "shajra.011": "Qutb-e-Samadani, Hazrat Shaikh Bu Ali Farmadi (RA)<small>477 AH — Farmad near Tus, Khorasan, Iran</small>", "shajra.012": "Rais-ut-Tareeqat, Ghaus-e-Zaman, Imam-e-Rabbani, Khwaja Yusuf Hamadani (RA)<small>535 AH — Merv, Iran</small>", "shajra.013": "Imam-ut-Tareeqat Khwaja-e-Jahan Khwaja Abdul Khaliq Ghujdawani (RA)<small>575 AH — Ghujdawan near Bukhara, Uzbekistan</small>", "shajra.014": "Noor-e-Khuda, Waqif-e-Maarif-e-Paighambari, Khwaja Arif Riwgari (RA)<small>616 AH — Riwgar near Bukhara, Uzbekistan</small>", "shajra.015": "Khwaja-e-Khwajgan, Qutb-e-Jahan, Hazrat Khwaja Mahmood Anjir Faghnawi (RA)<small>715 AH — Anjir Faghna near Bukhara</small>", "shajra.016": "Qutb-e-Zaman, Mujaddid-e-Dauran, Hazrat Khwaja Azizan Ali Ramitani (RA)<small>718 AH — Khwarazm, Uzbekistan</small>", "shajra.017": "Bab-ut-Tareeqat, Aftab-e-Haqeeqat Hazrat Khwaja Baba Muhammad Samasi (RA)<small>755 AH — Samas near Bukhara</small>", "shajra.018": "Arif-e-Ba-Kamal, Sahib-e-Wajd-o-Haal, Shams-ud-Din Sayyid Ameer Kulal (RA)<small>772 AH — Sukhar, Bukhara</small>", "shajra.019": "Imam-ut-Tareeqat Peer-e-Peeran Khwaja-e-Khwajgan Khwaja Bahauddin Naqshband (RA)<small>791 AH — Qasr-e-Arifan, Bukhara</small>", "shajra.020": "Imam-ul-Arifeen, Qutb-e-Irshad Hazrat Khwaja Alauddin Attar (RA)<small>802 AH — Chaghaniyan near Bukhara</small>", "shajra.021": "Shams-ul-Hidayat, Arif-e-Rabbani, Hazrat Maulana Muhammad Yaqub Charkhi (RA)<small>851 AH — Mawara-un-Nahr (Transoxiana), Tajikistan</small>", "shajra.022": "Murshid-e-Arif, Khwaja Nasir-ud-Din Ubaidullah Ahrar (RA)<small>895 AH — Samarkand, Uzbekistan</small>", "shajra.023": "Faiz-e-Ilahi, Yakta-e-Zamana, Hazrat Maulana Khwaja Muhammad Zahid Wakhshi (RA)<small>936 AH — Wakhsh, Balkh</small>", "shajra.024": "Mast-e-Ishq, Hazrat Maulana Khwaja Darvesh Muhammad Amkangi (RA)<small>970 AH — Mawara-un-Nahr (Transoxiana)</small>", "shajra.025": "Markaz-e-Daira-e-Qutbiyat, Darban-e-Rasool Maulana Shah Muhammad Khwajagi Amkangi (RA)<small>1008 AH — Amkana, Bukhara</small>", "shajra.026": "Fakhr-e-Islam, Naqshband-e-Waqt, Qutb-e-Zaman, Khwaja Muhammad Baqi Billah Berang (RA)<small>1012 AH — Delhi, India</small>", "shajra.027": "قیومِ اوّل، امامِ ربانی، مجدد الفِ ثانی، شیخ احمد فاروقی سرہندیؒ<small>1034 AH — Sirhind, India</small>", "shajra.028": "Qayyum-e-Sani, Urwat-ul-Wusqa Khwaja Muhammad Masoom (RA)<small>Son of Mujaddid Alf-e-Sani (RA) — 1079 AH — Sirhind Sharif</small>", "shajra.029": "Qati-e-Bid'at, Muhtasib-e-Ummat Shaikh Saif-ud-Din (RA)<small>Son of Qayyum-e-Sani (RA) — 1096 AH — Sirhind Sharif</small>", "shajra.030": "Kashf-ud-Duja Hazrat Hafiz Muhammad Mohsin (RA)<small>Khalifa of Khwaja Muhammad Masoom (RA) — 1147 AH — Delhi</small>", "shajra.031": "Hazrat Sayyid Noor Muhammad Badayuni (RA)<small>Khalifa of Shaikh Saif-ud-Din (RA) — 1135 AH — Delhi</small>", "shajra.032": "Qutb-e-Zaman Khwaja Muhammad Abid Sunami (RA)<small>Khalifa of Abdul Ahad Sirhindi Mujaddidi Qadiri (RA) — 1160 AH — Delhi</small>", "shajra.033": "Qayyum-e-Zaman, Qutb-e-Jahan, Shams-ud-Din Habibullah Mirza Mazhar Jan-e-Janan Shaheed (RA)<small>1195 AH — Delhi</small>", "shajra.034": "Mujaddid-e-Dauran, Qayyum-e-Zaman Hazrat Shah Abdullah Ghulam Ali Dehlvi (RA)<small>1240 AH — Delhi</small>", "shajra.035": "Shaikh-ul-Mashaikh, Qayyum-e-Zaman, Hazrat Shah Abu Saeed Farooqi Mujaddidi (RA)<small>1250 AH — Delhi</small>", "shajra.036": "Shams-ul-Awliya, Hazrat Maulana Baba Muhammad Sharif Qandhari (RA)<small>1260 AH — Sirhind Sharif</small>", "shajra.037": "Sultan-ul-Fuqara, Hazrat Haji Mahmood Jalandhari (RA)<small>1306 AH — Jalandhar Sharif, India</small>", "shajra.038": "Shams-ul-Irfan Khwaja Qadir Bakhsh (RA)<small>1306 AH — Kot Abdul Khaliq Jahankhel, District Hoshiarpur, India</small>", "shajra.039": "Shams-ul-Kaunain Khwaja Muhammad Abdul Khaliq Naqshbandi (RA)<small>1931 — Kot Abdul Khaliq Jahankhel, District Hoshiarpur, India</small>", "shajra.040": "Shams-ul-Arifeen Sain Abdul Razzaq Khaliqi Naqshbandi (RA)<small>1982 — Dipalpur Sharif, District Okara</small>", "shajra.041": "Imam-uz-Zakireen Huzoor Sain Muhammad Azeemullah Razzaqi Naqshbandi (RA)<small>2013 — Azeem Nagar Sharif, District Bahawalnagar</small>", "shajra.042": "Shajra Shareef (in verse)", "shajra.043": "It is strongly emphasised that this blessed Shajra be read with great reverence and in a state of wudu. While reading, make the heart present, focus on your lesson, keep your spiritual connection sound and seek spiritual grace from the great saints. This blessed Shajra is beloved and accepted by Huzoor Sayyid-e-Aalam Muhammad Mustafa ﷺ. The Holy Prophet, the Kind and Merciful ﷺ, accepting the humility of this servant of his servants, informed this faqeer in a dream that whoever reads this blessed Shajra with sincere intention, however great his difficulty, it will certainly be resolved, In sha Allah al-Aziz, through the blessing of the Khwajgan of the Naqshbandi order. After reading the Shajra Shareef, present your plea through the Holy Prophet ﷺ and pray to the Resolver of difficulties, the Causer of causes, the God of the worlds, for the resolution of difficulties.", "shajra.044": "Grant me help, for the sake of Muhammad Mustafa ﷺ,", "shajra.045": "for the sake of his family and companions and all the Prophets.", "shajra.046": "O God, grant my heart the pain of Your love,", "shajra.047": "for the sake of the pure Abu Bakr Siddiq-e-Akbar (RA).", "shajra.048": "O Lord, make me a kebab in Your love,", "shajra.049": "for the sake of the modest Salman (RA) of Persia, the Companion.", "shajra.050": "May all thoughts of anything besides Allah depart from my heart,", "shajra.051": "for the sake of that Imam Qasim (RA), the guide of guidance.", "shajra.052": "O God, save me from the evil of the disbelieving self (nafs),", "shajra.053": "for the sake of Jafar Sadiq (RA), the imam of the God-fearing.", "shajra.054": "O God, make me aware of the deceptions of Satan,", "shajra.055": "for the sake of that Bayazid (RA), the guide.", "shajra.056": "May I not be heedless of Your remembrance for even a single breath,", "shajra.057": "for the sake of Khwaja Abul Hasan (RA), the crown of the saints.", "shajra.058": "O Lord, make me annihilated (fana) in Your Absolute Essence,", "shajra.059": "for the sake of that king Abul Qasim (RA), the bearer of the banner.", "shajra.060": "O my Lord, do not make me other than the very Absolute Essence,", "shajra.061": "for the sake of Bu Ali (RA), the faithful Peer and Murshid.", "shajra.062": "Remove otherness from the heart and grant constant presence,", "shajra.063": "for the sake of Khwaja Yusuf (RA), the king whose prayers are accepted.", "shajra.064": "O Lord, may my soul pass from the copy into union with the Origin,", "shajra.065": "for the sake of Abdul Khaliq (RA) of Ghujdawan, intercessor for faults.", "shajra.066": "Grant me knowledge of the self so that I may recognise the Origin,", "shajra.067": "for the sake of that Muhammad Arif (RA), the light of God.", "shajra.068": "Make the circle of lovers encompassed by the Beloved,", "shajra.069": "for the sake of Khwaja Mahmood (RA) of Anjir (Faghna), the rich in spirit.", "shajra.070": "May this poor one rest at every moment in union with You,", "shajra.071": "for the sake of Shah Azizan (RA), (named) Ali Murtaza.", "shajra.072": "With a glance of mercy, forgive all my faults,", "shajra.073": "for the sake of Khwaja Baba Muhammad (RA) of graceful manner.", "shajra.074": "O God! Count me among the Ummah of Ahmad ﷺ,", "shajra.075": "for the sake of Sayyid Mir Kulal (RA), the content.", "shajra.076": "Keep me steadfast upon the Shariah and the Tareeqat,", "shajra.077": "for the sake of Shah Bahauddin (RA), the Khwaja and guide.", "shajra.078": "Grant lasting steadfastness upon the Straight Path,", "shajra.079": "for the sake of Shah Alauddin Attar (RA), the radiant.", "shajra.080": "O Lord, grant me love for my Peer,", "shajra.081": "for the sake of Khwaja Yaqub Charkhi (RA), the sincere.", "shajra.082": "O Lord, make me accepted in the sight of the noble Peers,", "shajra.083": "for the sake of that Ubaidullah Ahrar (RA), the generous.", "shajra.084": "Make the love of my Peer settle in my heart,", "shajra.085": "for the sake of Khwaja Zahid Muhammad (RA), the chosen.", "shajra.086": "O Lord, may my mind always remain on the counsel of the Peers,", "shajra.087": "for the sake of Khwaja Darvesh Muhammad (RA), the heart-winning.", "shajra.088": "O Generous Lord, grant trust (tawakkul) in my heart,", "shajra.089": "for the sake of Shah Muhammad Khwajagi (RA), the exalted.", "shajra.090": "Never make me grief-stricken in this world,", "shajra.091": "for the sake of that Muhammad Baqi Billah (RA), the everlasting.", "shajra.092": "O my God, do not make me dependent on anyone other than You,", "shajra.093": "for the sake of that Mujaddid Sahib (RA), the full moon in darkness.", "shajra.094": "When the time of death comes, may Your Kalima be upon my tongue,", "shajra.095": "for the sake of Hazrat Khwaja Masoom (RA), (O) Most Great.", "shajra.096": "Save me at that time from the evil of Satan,", "shajra.097": "for the sake of Shaikh Saif-ud-Din (RA), the lover of Mustafa ﷺ.", "shajra.098": "By Your grace, release me (with ease) in the throes of death,", "shajra.099": "for the sake of that Muhammad Abid (RA), the refuge of mankind.", "shajra.100": "O God, by Your grace may my grave be illuminated,", "shajra.101": "for the sake of Shah Muhammad Mohsin (RA), the dispeller of darkness.", "shajra.102": "May there be neither the hardship of the grave nor trouble from the angel,", "shajra.103": "for the sake of Sayyid Noor Muhammad (RA) of beautiful countenance.", "shajra.104": "When I walk upon the Bridge of Sirat, may the crossing be easy,", "shajra.105": "for the sake of Khwaja Mirza Jan-e-Janan (RA), the soul of our souls.", "shajra.106": "O Lord, grant safety at the time when Your sun is fierce,", "shajra.107": "for the sake of that Ghulam Shah Ali (RA), the morning sun.", "shajra.108": "O God, may the scale of good deeds in the Balance be heavy,", "shajra.109": "for the sake of Bu Saeed (RA), the guide of the pure ones.", "shajra.110": "O Creator of the world, may there be no disturbance at that moment,", "shajra.111": "for the sake of that Muhammad Sharif (RA), who sacrificed his life (in love).", "shajra.112": "O All-Knowing Lord, may my passage be among the lovers,", "shajra.113": "for the sake of Haji Mahmood Hafiz (RA), who opens hearts.", "shajra.114": "O Lord, may I remain under the shade of my Peer on the Day of Recompense,", "shajra.115": "for the sake of Khwaja Qadir Bakhsh (RA), the shade of the huma.", "shajra.116": "The heart aches from the fever of separation; grant it a cure,", "shajra.117": "for the sake of Shams-e-Irfan (RA), the cure for a burnt heart.", "shajra.118": "O my Lord, may union with the Beloved be my lot at every moment,", "shajra.119": "for the sake of the Khwaja of all Khwajgan (RA), of exalted praise.", "shajra.120": "I am in a poor state; O Lord, cast a glance of mercy,", "shajra.121": "for the sake of the beloved Murshid, the splendour of Mustafa ﷺ,", "shajra.122": "that is, the qibla of my soul, the Khwaja who is the refuge of the world,", "shajra.123": "for the sake of Shams-ul-Kaunain Abdul Khaliq (RA), the guide.", "shajra.124": "O my God, make me honourable in religion and in the world,", "shajra.125": "for the sake of my beloved Sain (RA), the Khwaja and guide.", "shajra.126": "Ghaus-e-Dauran, Qutb-e-Aalam, the enlightened Murshid,", "shajra.127": "for the sake of Sain Abdul Razzaq (RA), that imam of the saints.", "shajra.128": "O my Generous Lord, fill the lap of my hope,", "shajra.129": "for the sake of the perfect Peer, the image of the shadow of God.", "shajra.130": "Adorn my heart and sight with the light of faith,", "shajra.131": "for the sake of Shah Muhammad Azeemullah (RA), that light of God.", "shajra.132": "Who is there besides You? To whom shall I tell the pain of my heart?", "shajra.133": "You alone are the Fulfiller of needs for every wish.", "shajra.134": "O God, I face hundreds of hardships;", "shajra.135": "make them easy, for the sake of Your grandeur.", "shajra.136": "Though I am bad, I am Yours, O my Mighty and Majestic Lord;", "shajra.137": "Your mercy is needed for this helpless one.", "shajra.138": "O God, make my children fortunate,", "shajra.139": "for the sake of the generosity and gifts of the Prophets and saints.", "shajra.140": "Grant love to friends, relatives and kin,", "shajra.141": "for the sake of the family and the Two Sanctuaries of the Prophet, the leader ﷺ.", "shajra.142": "O God, accept the prayer of Your sinner,", "shajra.143": "for the sake of that honoured intercessor of the Day of Recompense ﷺ.", "azkar.001": "Sunnah Adhkar", "azkar.002": "Masnoon azkar after Fajr and Maghrib prayers", "azkar.003": "<p class=\"kk-ar\" lang=\"ar\">وَسَبِّحُوْهُ بُكْرَةً وَّاَصِيْلًا</p><p class=\"kk-ur\">And glorify Him morning and evening. (Surah Al-Ahzab: 42)</p>", "azkar.004": "Note: Our Imam-e-Rabbani Mujaddid Alf-e-Sani (RA) always recited the masnoon morning and evening azkar.", "azkar.005": "(There is no god but Allah Almighty, He is alone, He has no partner; His is the dominion and His is the praise, and He has power over all things.)", "azkar.006": "O Allah! Grant me deliverance from Hell.", "azkar.007": "Allah is sufficient for me; there is no god but Him; in Him I have put my trust, and He is the Lord of the Mighty Throne.", "azkar.008": "I put my trust in the One who is Ever-Living and never dies.", "azkar.009": "(Sahih Muslim)", "azkar.010": "6. Surah Al-Ikhlas and the Mu'awwidhatayn, with Bismillah <span class=\"kk-c\">3 times</span>", "azkar.011": "(Abu Dawud)", "azkar.012": "I am pleased with Allah Almighty as Lord, with Islam as religion, and with our master Hazrat Muhammad ﷺ as Prophet and Messenger.", "azkar.013": "(Jami' at-Tirmidhi)", "azkar.014": "In the name of Allah Almighty, by the blessing of whose name nothing in the earth or the heavens can cause harm, and He is the All-Hearing, the All-Knowing.", "azkar.015": "(Tirmidhi)", "azkar.016": "O Allah! Grant well-being to my body; O Allah! Grant well-being to my hearing; O Allah! Grant well-being to my sight. There is no god but You.", "azkar.017": "(Sahih Muslim)", "azkar.018": "I seek refuge in the complete and perfect words of Allah from the evil of what He has created.", "azkar.019": "(Sahih Muslim)", "azkar.020": "Masnoon azkar after the five daily prayers", "azkar.021": "<p class=\"kk-ar\" lang=\"ar\">فَاِذَا قَضَيْتُمُ الصَّلٰوةَ فَاذْكُرُوا اللّٰهَ قِيٰمًا وَّقُعُوْدًا وَّعَلٰى جُنُوْبِكُمْ</p><p class=\"kk-ur\">Then, when you have finished the prayer, remember Allah standing, sitting and lying on your sides. (Surah An-Nisa: 103)</p>", "azkar.022": "<p class=\"kk-ar\" lang=\"ar\">فَسَبِّحْهُ وَاَدْبَارَ السُّجُوْدِ</p><p class=\"kk-ur\">And glorify Him, and after the prayers as well. (Surah Qaf: 40)</p>", "azkar.023": "Note: Our Imam-e-Rabbani Mujaddid Alf-e-Sani (RA) recited the masnoon supplications after every prayer. While reciting the phrases, take care of tarteel, tajweed and the meanings. Recite Bismillah before every wird.", "azkar.024": "O Allah! You are Peace and from You is peace. Blessed are You, O Possessor of Majesty and Honour.", "azkar.025": "(Sahih Muslim)", "azkar.026": "3. Ayat-ul-Kursi", "azkar.027": "(Silsilat al-Ahadith as-Sahihah)", "azkar.028": "O Turner of hearts! Keep my heart firm upon Your religion and Your obedience.", "azkar.029": "(Tirmidhi)", "azkar.030": "Our Lord! Do not let our hearts deviate after You have guided us, and grant us mercy from Yourself; indeed You are the Bestower.", "azkar.031": "(Ibn Majah) (Surah Aal-e-Imran: 8)", "azkar.032": "O Allah! Help me to remember You, to thank You and to worship You in the best manner.", "azkar.033": "(Abu Dawud)", "azkar.034": "O Ever-Living, O Sustainer! There is no god but You. I ask that You keep my heart alive forever with the light of Your gnosis. O Possessor of great Majesty and Honour! You are pure.", "azkar.035": "(Kanz al-Ummal)", "azkar.036": "8. Tasbeeh-e-Fatimah", "azkar.037": "SubhanAllah 33 times, Alhamdulillah 33 times, Allahu Akbar 33 times, and the Kalima of Tawheed once.", "azkar.038": "(Sahih Muslim)", "azkar.039": "(Tirmidhi)", "azkar.040": "10. Kalima-e-Tamjeed", "azkar.041": "11. The three Quls", "azkar.042": "11. Surah Al-Ikhlas <span class=\"kk-c\">10 times</span>", "azkar.043": "(Musnad Ahmad)", "azkar.044": "Short Khatm-e-Khwajgan", "azkar.045": "Make it a routine to recite the following short Khatm-e-Khwajgan after the Fajr prayer and after the Asr prayer.", "azkar.046": "1. Astaghfirullah <span class=\"kk-c\">26 times</span>", "azkar.047": "2. Surah Al-Fatihah <span class=\"kk-c\">7 times</span>", "azkar.048": "3. Durood Shareef <span class=\"kk-c\">11 times</span>", "azkar.049": "Additional masnoon supplications of prayer", "azkar.050": "Note: Urwat-ul-Wusqa Khwaja Muhammad Masoom Sirhindi (RA) says that, besides the Thana, the transmitted supplications for opening the prayer, and likewise, besides the tasbeehat, the supplications of ruku and sujood and of qauma and jalsa mentioned in the blessed hadiths — reciting them in Tahajjud and other voluntary prayers is very good; and in the final sitting (qa'dah), after Durood Shareef, recite Quranic supplications or transmitted, masnoon supplications. As in the hadith in Sahih Bukhari: Then let him make whatever supplication he likes. (Azkar-e-Nabawiyya)", "azkar.051": "Allah is the Greatest, truly great; much praise belongs to Allah; and I glorify Allah morning and evening. Hazrat Jubayr ibn Mut'im (RA) relates that he saw the Prophet ﷺ offering a prayer, and he ﷺ recited these words at the start of the prayer.", "azkar.052": "(Sunan Abu Dawud)", "azkar.053": "Most Pure, Most Holy, Lord of the angels and of the Spirit. Reciting these words in ruku and sujood is Sunnah. The Prophet ﷺ said: A servant is closest to his Lord while in prostration, so make abundant supplication in prostration.", "azkar.054": "(Sahih Muslim)", "azkar.055": "Note: In his free time, our Imam-e-Rabbani Mujaddid Alf-e-Sani (RA) recited the tasbeehat five, seven, nine or eleven times in ruku and sujood, and used to say: I feel ashamed that, despite having strength and being free, one should suffice with only three tasbeehat. (Hazarat-ul-Quds)", "azkar.056": "O my Lord! All praise is for You — praise that is abundant, pure and blessed. O our Lord! As You like and as pleases You. In qauma, after raising the head from ruku, reciting these words, especially in voluntary prayer, is Sunnah.", "azkar.057": "(Bukhari)", "azkar.058": "O Allah! Forgive me, have mercy on me, guide me, provide for me, raise my rank, set right my affairs and grant me well-being. Reciting these words in jalsa between the two prostrations, especially in voluntary prayer, is Sunnah.", "azkar.059": "(Sunan Abu Dawud, Tirmidhi)", "azkar.060": "Masnoon azkar at the time of rest", "azkar.061": "In Surah Az-Zumar Allah says: Allah takes the souls at the time of their death, and also those that have not died, during their sleep. (42)", "azkar.062": "<p class=\"kk-ar\" lang=\"ar\">وَسَبِّحْهُ لَيْلًا طَوِيْلًا</p><p class=\"kk-ur\">In Surah Ad-Dahr it is said: And glorify Him through the long night. (26)</p>", "azkar.063": "The Holy Prophet ﷺ said: Some people in the world remember Allah Almighty on soft beds; Allah Almighty will admit them to the highest Paradise. (Musannaf Abi Yusuf). Whoever lies on a bed or sits in a gathering in which he does not remember Allah Almighty, it will be a cause of regret for him on the Day of Judgement. (Abu Dawud)", "azkar.064": "Note: Our Imam-e-Rabbani (RA) recited surahs, verses, tasbeehat and transmitted supplications at bedtime.", "azkar.065": "The Holy Prophet ﷺ said to Sayyiduna Ali al-Murtaza (RA): O Ali (RA)! Do five things before you sleep:", "azkar.066": "1. Surah Al-Fatihah <span class=\"kk-c\">4 times</span>", "azkar.067": "Recite it four times before sleeping; it is equal to giving four thousand dinars in charity.", "azkar.068": "2. Surah Al-Ikhlas <span class=\"kk-c\">3 times</span>", "azkar.069": "Recite it three times before sleeping; it is equal to reciting the whole Holy Quran once.", "azkar.070": "Recite it ten times before sleeping; its reward is equal to making peace between two who are quarrelling.", "azkar.071": "4. Durood Shareef <span class=\"kk-c\">10 times</span>", "azkar.072": "Recite it ten times before sleeping; it is equal to paying the price of Paradise.", "azkar.073": "5. Kalima-e-Tamjeed <span class=\"kk-c\">4 times</span>", "azkar.074": "Recite it four times before sleeping; it is equal to performing one Hajj.", "azkar.075": "6. Surah Al-Kafirun <span class=\"kk-c\">Once</span>", "azkar.076": "Hazrat Nawfal (RA) says that the Holy Prophet ﷺ told me: Recite Surah Al-Kafirun before sleeping, for it is a declaration of freedom from shirk.", "azkar.077": "(Abu Dawud)", "azkar.078": "7. The three Quls <span class=\"kk-c\">3 times</span>", "azkar.079": "Umm-ul-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (RA) says that when the Holy Prophet ﷺ came to his bed to rest, he would join both hands, recite Surah Al-Ikhlas, Al-Falaq and An-Nas, blow into them, and pass his hands over as much of his blessed body as they could reach, beginning with the head and face; and he did this three times.", "azkar.080": "(Sahih Bukhari)", "azkar.081": "The Prophet ﷺ said: Whoever recites this istighfar three times when lying down on his bed, his sins are forgiven, even if they are like the foam of the sea, even if like the leaves of the trees, even if like the grains of sand of the dunes, even if like the days of the world.", "azkar.082": "(Tirmidhi)", "azkar.083": "9. Ayat-ul-Kursi", "azkar.084": "The Prophet ﷺ said: Whoever recites Ayat-ul-Kursi at bedtime, an angel is appointed to protect him and Satan does not come near him until morning. (Bukhari) Whoever recites it lying on his bed, Allah Almighty protects several houses around him.", "azkar.085": "10. Bismillah Shareef <span class=\"kk-c\">21 times</span>", "azkar.086": "The Holy Prophet ﷺ said that whoever recites Bismillah 21 times before sleeping will remain safe from theft, satanic influences and sudden death.", "azkar.087": "11. Tasbeeh-e-Fatimah", "azkar.088": "(Muttafaq Alayh)", "azkar.089": "12. Supplication for sleep", "azkar.090": "O Allah! In Your name I die and in Your name I live.", "azkar.091": "(Muttafaq Alayh)", "azkar.092": "13. The last two verses of Surah Al-Baqarah", "azkar.093": "Masnoon azkar of Friday night and Friday", "azkar.094": "Note: Our Imam-e-Rabbani Mujaddid Alf-e-Sani (RA) abundantly sent various kinds of Durood Shareef to the court of the Holy Prophet ﷺ, especially on Friday night and Friday, and on Monday night and Monday. In his later years, on Friday night, after the circle of zikr with the mureeds, he sent Durood Shareef a thousand times.", "azkar.095": "1. Durood Shareef for Friday night <span class=\"kk-c\">A thousand times</span>", "azkar.096": "2. Durood Shareef after Jumu'ah <span class=\"kk-c\">A thousand times</span>", "azkar.097": "Shaikh Abdul Qadir Jilani (RA) has advised reciting this Durood Shareef on Friday in Ghunyat-ut-Talibeen.", "azkar.098": "3. Durood Shareef after the Asr prayer <span class=\"kk-c\">80 times</span>", "azkar.099": "A saying of the Prophet ﷺ narrated by Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (RA): Whoever, on Friday, after praying Asr, recites this Durood-e-Pak 80 times while sitting in the same place, 80 years of his sins will be forgiven and the reward of 80 years of worship is written in his record of deeds.", "azkar.100": "(Daylami, Imam Sakhawi)", "azkar.101": "4. Kimiya-e-Mashaikh", "azkar.102": "Shaikh Abdul Haq Muhaddith Dehlvi (RA) has written a proven wazifa, «Kimiya-e-Mashaikh», for the forgiveness of past and future sins: after the salam of the Jumu'ah prayer, while sitting in the tashahhud posture, recite Surah Al-Fatihah and the three Quls, with Bismillah, seven times each. It is in the hadith that reciting these surahs gives protection from Satan from this Friday to the next Friday.", "azkar.103": "(Kimiya-e-Sa'adat)", "azkar.104": "Note: After the Jumu'ah prayer, Imam-e-Rabbani (RA) recited Surah Al-Fatihah and the three Quls, with Bismillah, seven times each.", "azkar.105": "<p class=\"kk-ar\" lang=\"ar\">فَاِذَا قُضِيَتِ الصَّلٰوةُ فَانْتَشِرُوْا فِي الْاَرْضِ وَابْتَغُوْا مِنْ فَضْلِ اللّٰهِ</p><p class=\"kk-ur\">Then, when the prayer is finished, disperse in the land and seek the bounty of Allah. (Surah Al-Jumu'ah: 10)</p>", "azkar.106": "Hazrat Anas (RA) says: Buying, selling and earning worldly gain are not the meaning of this verse; rather, seeking knowledge, visiting brothers, visiting the sick, accompanying a funeral, and any such good deeds are what this verse means. Because Allah Almighty says further on in Surah Al-Jumu'ah:", "azkar.107": "<p class=\"kk-ar\" lang=\"ar\">وَاذْكُرُوا اللّٰهَ كَثِيْرًا لَّعَلَّكُمْ تُفْلِحُوْنَ</p><p class=\"kk-ur\">And remember Allah abundantly so that you may succeed.</p>", "programs.001": "Annual Programmes", "atiyat.001": "Donations", "atiyat.002": "For those who wish to support the religious and reformative services of the Tehreek — may Allah accept it.", "rabta.001": "Contact", "about.001": "About App", "kutub.020": "Khauf-e-Khuda aur Ishq-e-Mustafa ﷺ", "kutub.021": "<span>Author:</span> Founder and Leader of Tehreek Ittiba-e-Sunnat Pakistan, Peer-e-Tareeqat, Sher-e-Mujaddid Badr-ul-Huda Karamat Ali Razzaqi Azeemi Naqshbandi <span class=\"lat\">(M.A, L.L.B)</span>", "kutub.022": "<span>Assisted by:</span> Engineer Shoaib Alam Azeemi Mujaddidi (M.A. Islamic Studies), <span class=\"lat\">HOD</span> Electrical Trade, Government Technical Training Institute Lodhran", "kutub.023": "Pages: <span class=\"lat\">128</span>  • Published: December <span class=\"lat\">2019</span> (Second Edition)"};
